ltiplies discoverable surface area per chapter at near-zero marginal cost; DA and future Twitter/IG get full stories instead of crops, which is where the niche&#x27;s top funnels (MaxxMuscleComics-style free-first releases) get their subscribers.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion — bigger public funnel feeding paywalled explicit editions</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comic-production genspec + QA chain; syndicator destinations; beyond public teaser pages w/ UTM</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="market" data-eff="S" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="patreon collections binge-merchandising pass (gwhar-owned) the observed premium-tier playbook includes &#x27;organized folders with complete stories in one place, ready to read/download&#x27;, and patreon&#x27;s collections feature plus manual back-catalog entitlements make this pure merchandising work. audit all 4 accounts: build per-series collections in reading order, pin a &#x27;start here&#x27; guide post, and verify every old post&#x27;s tier entitlement actually matches the current ladder. assign to gwhar — he loves finding and reading stories, and this is exactly that. distinct from the vault tier pilot: no new pricing, just making the catalog bingeable so the tiers sell themselves. binge depth is the quiet retention lever — new patrons who binge a full series in week one retain far better than ones who see a wall of unsorted posts; also prerequisite plumbing for the all-access library flagship."><summary><span class="t">Patreon Collections binge-merchandising pass (GWHAR-owned)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Market Intel</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:GWHAR</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The observed premium-tier playbook includes &#x27;organized folders with complete stories in one place, ready to read/download&#x27;, and Patreon&#x27;s Collections feature plus manual back-catalog entitlements make this pure merchandising work. Audit all 4 accounts: build per-series Collections in reading order, pin a &#x27;start here&#x27; guide post, and verify every old post&#x27;s tier entitlement actually matches the current ladder. Assign to GWHAR — he loves finding and reading stories, and this is exactly that. Distinct from the Vault tier pilot: no new pricing, just making the catalog bingeable so the tiers sell themselves.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Binge depth is the quiet retention lever — new patrons who binge a full series in week one retain far better than ones who see a wall of unsorted posts; also prerequisite plumbing for the all-access library flagship.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention — onboarding/binge experience across 4 accounts</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Feeds the all-access member library flagship; GWHAR story-scout role</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="market" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="fanbox (pixiv) japanese edition channel riding the translation factory pixivfanbox pays 90% to the creator, and the muscle-growth/kinniku niche has a substantial japanese audience already congregating on pixiv. extend the existing es/de/zh translation conveyor with a ja job kind, open one fanbox at ¥500/¥1000 tiers, and post monthly ja editions with pixiv gallery posts as the discovery layer. builds on the excluded translation conveyor rather than re-proposing it: the conveyor is the machine; this is a new paid distribution endpoint and market. a fifth-language market at the best revenue split observed anywhere (90%); even 40 jp members at ~$6 net is ~$215/mo from content the conveyor produces essentially free."><summary><span class="t">Fanbox (pixiv) Japanese edition channel riding the translation factory</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Market Intel</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>pixivFANBOX pays 90% to the creator, and the muscle-growth/kinniku niche has a substantial Japanese audience already congregating on pixiv. Extend the existing ES/DE/ZH translation conveyor with a JA job kind, open one Fanbox at ¥500/¥1000 tiers, and post monthly JA editions with pixiv gallery posts as the discovery layer. Builds on the excluded translation conveyor rather than re-proposing it: the conveyor is the machine; this is a new paid distribution endpoint and market.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> A fifth-language market at the best revenue split observed anywhere (90%); even 40 JP members at ~$6 net is ~$215/mo from content the conveyor produces essentially free.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — new geography at a 90% platform split</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Translation conveyor (new JA job kind), Alternate posting workflow</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="market" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="niche competitor-intel tracker (studio/market.php) this wave&#x27;s research shows the pricing intel is public and decision-grade — graphtreon patron counts and public creator pages expose competitors&#x27; prices and cadence (amazing transformations $11/$14, muscle fan $19.95, mg komiks weekly cadence, z-pico, reiner55, giorunog). build a monthly scraper into a small studio/market.php section tracking ~15 named niche competitors: patron count, tier prices, posts/month, platform stack changes. surface a monthly &#x27;pricing review&#x27; card into the command center so repricing becomes a ritual instead of a one-off. the gap this very lens found — competitors charging 2-4x typical entry tiers — is what the tracker institutionalizes; one justified $1 price move at 400 patrons pays for it 50x over."><summary><span class="t">Niche competitor-intel tracker (studio/market.php)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Market Intel</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>This wave&#x27;s research shows the pricing intel is public and decision-grade — Graphtreon patron counts and public creator pages expose competitors&#x27; prices and cadence (Amazing Transformations $11/$14, Muscle Fan $19.95, MG Komiks weekly cadence, Z-Pico, reiner55, giorunog). Build a monthly scraper into a small studio/market.php section tracking ~15 named niche competitors: patron count, tier prices, posts/month, platform stack changes. Surface a monthly &#x27;pricing review&#x27; card into the Command Center so repricing becomes a ritual instead of a one-off.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The gap this very lens found — competitors charging 2-4x typical entry tiers — is what the tracker institutionalizes; one justified $1 price move at 400 patrons pays for it 50x over.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU — keeps pricing benchmarked to the niche norm continuously</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Studio PHP infra, cc.php Command Center cards, Mac mini daily-sync pattern from Creator Pulse</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="market" data-eff="S" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="producer&#x27;s circle: 10 capped cameo seats at $29/mo adult-game top tiers monetize fans &#x27;becoming part of the creation process&#x27;, and amazing transformations sells commissioning votes at its top tier — the scarcity version is stronger. sell exactly 10 &#x27;producer&#x27; seats at $29/mo on growgetter: each producer gets a requested character or self-insert cameo woven into a canon chapter each month (subject to content rules), plus name-in-credits on the chapter page. cameos slot into already-planned chapters via a one-line genspec addition, so marginal cost is near zero. goes beyond the excluded monthly story polls: this is a scarcity-priced personal product, not a vote. 10 seats × $29 = $290/mo guaranteed recurring at near-zero marginal cost, with a waitlist mechanic that makes the flagship feel oversubscribed; producers are also the least likely members to ever churn."><summary><span class="t">Producer&#x27;s Circle: 10 capped cameo seats at $29/mo</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Market Intel</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Adult-game top tiers monetize fans &#x27;becoming part of the creation process&#x27;, and Amazing Transformations sells commissioning votes at its top tier — the scarcity version is stronger. Sell exactly 10 &#x27;Producer&#x27; seats at $29/mo on GrowGetter: each producer gets a requested character or self-insert cameo woven into a canon chapter each month (subject to content rules), plus name-in-credits on the chapter page. Cameos slot into already-planned chapters via a one-line genspec addition, so marginal cost is near zero. Goes beyond the excluded monthly story polls: this is a scarcity-priced personal product, not a vote.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> 10 seats × $29 = $290/mo guaranteed recurring at near-zero marginal cost, with a waitlist mechanic that makes the flagship feel oversubscribed; producers are also the least likely members to ever churn.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU — scarcity-priced top tier with personal content</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Beyond monthly patron story polls; genspec cameo field + QA chain, chapter credits on comics.js pages</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="scale"><h3>Scale-Up <span class="n">16</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="launch 3dgiantesscomics as property #6 (giantess growth vertical) the scaffold site and sandboxed deploy.sh already exist — the pipeline just needs a cast. phase 1 (wk 1-2): lock 2 giantess leads with character sheets + size-stage guides, deploy the scaffold, spin up a dedicated patreon + deviantart account. phase 2 (wk 3-5): produce a 3-chapter launch arc via the proven overnight autonomous run, seeding the site with a free chapter 1. phase 3 (wk 6+): move to biweekly cadence via bridge.php worker jobs and cross-promo from the muscle properties (adjacent audience, high overlap in size-kink readers). giantess is a larger, better-monetized kink niche than fmg. even a modest 100-150 patrons at ~$5 avg within 6 months is $500-750/mo of purely incremental mrr, with near-zero marginal art cost."><summary><span class="t">Launch 3dgiantesscomics as Property #6 (giantess growth vertical)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The scaffold site and sandboxed deploy.sh already exist — the pipeline just needs a cast. Phase 1 (wk 1-2): lock 2 giantess leads with character sheets + size-stage guides, deploy the scaffold, spin up a dedicated Patreon + DeviantArt account. Phase 2 (wk 3-5): produce a 3-chapter launch arc via the proven overnight autonomous run, seeding the site with a free chapter 1. Phase 3 (wk 6+): move to biweekly cadence via bridge.php worker jobs and cross-promo from the muscle properties (adjacent audience, high overlap in size-kink readers).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Giantess is a larger, better-monetized kink niche than FMG. Even a modest 100-150 patrons at ~$5 avg within 6 months is $500-750/mo of purely incremental MRR, with near-zero marginal art cost.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — 5th/6th Patreon account in an adjacent kink with a distinct audience</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> 3dgiantesscomics scaffold + sandboxed deploy.sh, comic-production pipeline character-lock system, bridge.php worker protocol</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="launch a male muscle-growth property (property #7) male mg is a large, distinct market (gay muscle-growth patreons routinely clear $2-5k/mo) and the pipeline is kink-agnostic — only refs and prompt anchors change. phase 1 (wk 1): market scan of the top 10 male-mg creators for pricing/format norms. phase 2 (wk 2-4): lock a 2-3 man cast with size-stage guides, produce a 3-chapter pilot arc overnight, validate render quality on male anatomy (over-spec compensation lessons transfer). phase 3 (wk 5-8): dedicated patreon + da, biweekly cadence, zero cross-promo dependency since the audience barely overlaps fmg. fully incremental audience. a conservative 100 patrons × $6 within 6-9 months is $600/mo; the niche&#x27;s proven ceiling is several thousand/mo for consistent weekly output — which the runner makes trivial."><summary><span class="t">Launch a male muscle-growth property (Property #7)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Male MG is a large, distinct market (gay muscle-growth Patreons routinely clear $2-5k/mo) and the pipeline is kink-agnostic — only refs and prompt anchors change. Phase 1 (wk 1): market scan of the top 10 male-MG creators for pricing/format norms. Phase 2 (wk 2-4): lock a 2-3 man cast with size-stage guides, produce a 3-chapter pilot arc overnight, validate render quality on male anatomy (over-spec compensation lessons transfer). Phase 3 (wk 5-8): dedicated Patreon + DA, biweekly cadence, zero cross-promo dependency since the audience barely overlaps FMG.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Fully incremental audience. A conservative 100 patrons × $6 within 6-9 months is $600/mo; the niche&#x27;s proven ceiling is several thousand/mo for consistent weekly output — which the runner makes trivial.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — new Patreon in a non-overlapping, high-monetization niche</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comic-production pipeline + 35 codified lessons, over-spec size compensation lessons, Creator Pulse multi-account rollup (add 5th account)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="weekly-cadence lock: guaranteed release day on all 4 properties, backed by a 4-week buffer bank turn raw runner capacity into a subscription promise: &#x27;every friday, no exceptions&#x27; per property. phase 1 (wk 1-3): burn runner nights to build a 4-chapter buffer per property (16 chapters banked). phase 2 (wk 4): publish the release calendar on every patreon and the site; add a buffer-depth gauge to creator pulse so a property never drops below 2 banked chapters without triggering a production job. phase 3: alternate posts from the bank on schedule — the buffer decouples production hiccups from the audience-facing promise. predictable cadence is the #1 churn lever on patreon (&#x27;what did i pay for this month?&#x27;). cutting monthly churn from ~8% to ~6% raises average patron ltv ~33% (ltv = arpu/churn: $5/0.08=$62 → $5/0.06=$83); at 500 patrons that compounds to hundreds/mo within two quarters."><summary><span class="t">Weekly-cadence lock: guaranteed release day on all 4 properties, backed by a 4-week buffer bank</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Turn raw runner capacity into a subscription promise: &#x27;every Friday, no exceptions&#x27; per property. Phase 1 (wk 1-3): burn runner nights to build a 4-chapter buffer per property (16 chapters banked). Phase 2 (wk 4): publish the release calendar on every Patreon and the site; add a buffer-depth gauge to Creator Pulse so a property never drops below 2 banked chapters without triggering a production job. Phase 3: Alternate posts from the bank on schedule — the buffer decouples production hiccups from the audience-facing promise.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Predictable cadence is the #1 churn lever on Patreon (&#x27;what did I pay for this month?&#x27;). Cutting monthly churn from ~8% to ~6% raises average patron LTV ~33% (LTV = ARPU/churn: $5/0.08=$62 → $5/0.06=$83); at 500 patrons that compounds to hundreds/mo within two quarters.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention — churn reduction via predictable release rhythm; also lifts conversion (visible active schedule)</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Goes beyond the Night Shift runner (execution layer) — this is the editorial buffer system + public cadence SLA on top; Creator Pulse for buffer gauge; Alternate handles posting</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="webtoon vertical reformat conveyor + sfw serialization channel on webtoon canvas/tapas page-composer already knows every panel&#x27;s geometry and the shotlist holds all dialogue — a reformatter that slices pages into panel crops and restacks them as infinite-canvas vertical strips is mostly plumbing. phase 1 (wk 1-3): build the vertical-stack composer (panel crops, re-flowed bubbles from shotlist data, episode chunking ~40-60 panels). phase 2 (wk 4-5): reformat growgetter season 1 as an sfw-trimmed serialization, publish weekly on webtoon canvas + tapas with end-cards pointing to patreon. phase 3: fold the reformatter into the pipeline so every new chapter emits a vertical edition automatically. opens a mobile-native discovery channel the niche barely uses, at near-zero marginal cost per chapter. canvas hits of even modest size drive thousands of impressions/wk; a 0.5% click-through to patreon at 10k weekly readers is ~50 warm leads/mo."><summary><span class="t">Webtoon vertical reformat conveyor + SFW serialization channel on Webtoon Canvas/Tapas</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>page-composer already knows every panel&#x27;s geometry and the shotlist holds all dialogue — a reformatter that slices pages into panel crops and restacks them as infinite-canvas vertical strips is mostly plumbing. Phase 1 (wk 1-3): build the vertical-stack composer (panel crops, re-flowed bubbles from shotlist data, episode chunking ~40-60 panels). Phase 2 (wk 4-5): reformat GrowGetter Season 1 as an SFW-trimmed serialization, publish weekly on Webtoon Canvas + Tapas with end-cards pointing to Patreon. Phase 3: fold the reformatter into the pipeline so every new chapter emits a vertical edition automatically.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Opens a mobile-native discovery channel the niche barely uses, at near-zero marginal cost per chapter. Canvas hits of even modest size drive thousands of impressions/wk; a 0.5% click-through to Patreon at 10k weekly readers is ~50 warm leads/mo.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion — top-of-funnel discovery on platforms with built-in audiences</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> page-composer panel-geometry + lettering data, script-breakdown shotlists; complements (does not duplicate) the excluded teaser-page/syndicator ideas — this is a format conversion engine, not a posting tool</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="remastered editions program: industrialize the 2d→3d importer across the oldest catalog explicitly beyond the excluded comic redactor re-release engine (which re-posts existing pages) — this produces genuinely new art from old 2d comics using the proven import.php pipeline, sold as new releases. phase 1 (wk 1): poll patrons for the top-5 most-wanted classic titles. phase 2 (wk 2-6): run one remaster per week through import.php (pdf→snip→dialogue→i2i with stage-aware refs), qa-gated, released as &#x27;remastered edition&#x27; premium chapters. phase 3 (wk 7+): package each finished remaster series as a sellable bundle and keep a standing one-remaster-per-week slot in the runner. converts a dormant back catalog into a new-release stream with zero writing cost. a 20-title backlog is ~5 months of extra weekly &#x27;new&#x27; releases; remaster bundles at $10-15 to non-patrons plausibly add $300-600/mo."><summary><span class="t">Remastered Editions program: industrialize the 2D→3D importer across the oldest catalog</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream + retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Explicitly beyond the excluded Comic Redactor re-release engine (which re-posts existing pages) — this produces genuinely NEW art from old 2D comics using the proven import.php pipeline, sold as new releases. Phase 1 (wk 1): poll patrons for the top-5 most-wanted classic titles. Phase 2 (wk 2-6): run one remaster per week through import.php (PDF→snip→dialogue→i2i with stage-aware refs), QA-gated, released as &#x27;Remastered Edition&#x27; premium chapters. Phase 3 (wk 7+): package each finished remaster series as a sellable bundle and keep a standing one-remaster-per-week slot in the runner.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts a dormant back catalog into a new-release stream with zero writing cost. A 20-title backlog is ~5 months of extra weekly &#x27;new&#x27; releases; remaster bundles at $10-15 to non-patrons plausibly add $300-600/mo.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream + retention — new releases from old IP; remaster bundles as one-time products</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> import.php 2D→3D importer (proven), Müller 02 as the template run, QA gate chain</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="guest-writer publishing program: sign established da/forum fmg writers for rev-share comic adaptations goes beyond the excluded gwhar story-scout intake (which finds stories) — this is a full publisher model: deviantart and forum fmg *prose* writers with existing followings get their stories turned into comics they could never afford to commission ($1000+ and months with human artists). phase 1 (wk 1-2): gwhar builds a shortlist of 10 writers with 500+ watchers; owner sends offers (flat $100 or 20% rev-share on the release). phase 2 (wk 3-5): produce 2 pilot adaptations via script-breakdown → overnight run, credited prominently. phase 3: writers announce to their own audiences — every guest story imports a warm audience; formalize a rolling 1-guest-story-per-month slot. each signed writer is both free script supply and a marketing channel. two guest releases/mo, each pulling even 15-25 new patrons from the writer&#x27;s audience at $5, is $150-250/mo of compounding mrr plus a widening moat as &#x27;the publisher&#x27; of the niche."><summary><span class="t">Guest-writer publishing program: sign established DA/forum FMG writers for rev-share comic adaptations</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion + new stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the excluded GWHAR story-scout intake (which finds stories) — this is a full publisher model: DeviantArt and forum FMG *prose* writers with existing followings get their stories turned into comics they could never afford to commission ($1000+ and months with human artists). Phase 1 (wk 1-2): GWHAR builds a shortlist of 10 writers with 500+ watchers; owner sends offers (flat $100 or 20% rev-share on the release). Phase 2 (wk 3-5): produce 2 pilot adaptations via script-breakdown → overnight run, credited prominently. Phase 3: writers announce to their own audiences — every guest story imports a warm audience; formalize a rolling 1-guest-story-per-month slot.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Each signed writer is both free script supply and a marketing channel. Two guest releases/mo, each pulling even 15-25 new patrons from the writer&#x27;s audience at $5, is $150-250/mo of compounding MRR plus a widening moat as &#x27;the publisher&#x27; of the niche.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion + new stream — imported audiences per guest writer; positions 3DMC as the niche&#x27;s publisher</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> GWHAR story-scout intake (beyond), script-breakdown skill, overnight autonomous production run</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="cross-property crossover event: one story arc spanning all 4 patreon accounts a &#x27;growth wars&#x27;-style event only an ai pipeline can afford: the growgetter, maxx, bloom, and poweredheroes casts collide in a 4-part arc where each part releases on a different patreon account. phase 1 (wk 1-2): event outline + a unified cast lineup sheet merging all four properties&#x27; character locks. phase 2 (wk 3-6): produce all 4 chapters (continuity-check across the whole event, one shared size-guide). phase 3 (wk 7-8): staggered weekly release with each chapter ending on a cliffhanger resolved on the next account; free recap pages on the site so single-account patrons feel the pull, not a paywall slap. directly engineers multi-account subscription. if 10% of a 500-patron base adds one extra $5 account for the event and half stick, that is ~$125/mo permanent arpu lift — repeatable as an annual event."><summary><span class="t">Cross-property crossover event: one story arc spanning all 4 Patreon accounts</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A &#x27;Growth Wars&#x27;-style event only an AI pipeline can afford: the GrowGetter, Maxx, Bloom, and PoweredHeroes casts collide in a 4-part arc where each part releases on a DIFFERENT Patreon account. Phase 1 (wk 1-2): event outline + a unified cast lineup sheet merging all four properties&#x27; character locks. Phase 2 (wk 3-6): produce all 4 chapters (continuity-check across the whole event, one shared size-guide). Phase 3 (wk 7-8): staggered weekly release with each chapter ending on a cliffhanger resolved on the next account; free recap pages on the site so single-account patrons feel the pull, not a paywall slap.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Directly engineers multi-account subscription. If 10% of a 500-patron base adds one extra $5 account for the event and half stick, that is ~$125/mo permanent ARPU lift — repeatable as an annual event.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU — converts single-account patrons into multi-account patrons</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> All four properties&#x27; character locks + cast-lineup style propagation, continuity-check skill, 4-account Creator Pulse to measure cross-sub lift</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="L" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="animated edition upsell tier (seedance motion comics per release) the müller 02 run proved 47 panels → 18 clips is routine. productize it: every flagship chapter ships a 60-90 second animated edition (key growth beats animated, mini 480p for iteration, std for finals) gated behind a +$3-5 &#x27;motion&#x27; tier on growgetter&#x27;s patreon. standardize a per-chapter shotlist template (the 5-6 highest growth-density panels only) so each edition is one overnight batch. pilot on 3 releases before wiring the tier permanently. pure arpu: at 300 growgetter patrons with a 15% attach rate on a +$4 tier, ~$180/mo, scaling with patron count. animated growth content is nearly nonexistent in the niche — strong differentiation."><summary><span class="t">Animated Edition upsell tier (Seedance motion comics per release)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The Müller 02 run proved 47 panels → 18 clips is routine. Productize it: every flagship chapter ships a 60-90 second Animated Edition (key growth beats animated, mini 480p for iteration, std for finals) gated behind a +$3-5 &#x27;Motion&#x27; tier on GrowGetter&#x27;s Patreon. Standardize a per-chapter shotlist template (the 5-6 highest growth-density panels only) so each edition is one overnight batch. Pilot on 3 releases before wiring the tier permanently.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Pure ARPU: at 300 GrowGetter patrons with a 15% attach rate on a +$4 tier, ~$180/mo, scaling with patron count. Animated growth content is nearly nonexistent in the niche — strong differentiation.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU — premium format tier on existing releases</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Seedance video pipeline + Müller 02 shotlist template, add-video.sh site video pages; distinct from the excluded auto-trailer (marketing asset) — this is a paid product tier</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="productized custom-chapter commissions with a 7-day turnaround sla beyond the excluded commission intake funnel (the form) — this is the offering itself: fixed skus (&#x27;10-page custom fmg chapter, your premise, your character description: $300; 20 pages: $500&#x27;) fulfilled via the proven overnight run, with a public 7-day delivery promise no human artist can match ($1000+ and 2-6 month queues are the norm). includes a standard revision pass powered by the qa defect scan, a per-order genspec template, and a cap of 4 slots/month to protect the release schedule. turns &#x27;occasional commissions&#x27; into a listed product line. 3 orders/mo × $350 avg = ~$1,050/mo at maybe 2 hours of human time per order; the turnaround sla is itself the marketing hook."><summary><span class="t">Productized custom-chapter commissions with a 7-day turnaround SLA</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Beyond the excluded commission intake funnel (the form) — this is the offering itself: fixed SKUs (&#x27;10-page custom FMG chapter, your premise, your character description: $300; 20 pages: $500&#x27;) fulfilled via the proven overnight run, with a public 7-day delivery promise no human artist can match ($1000+ and 2-6 month queues are the norm). Includes a standard revision pass powered by the QA defect scan, a per-order genspec template, and a cap of 4 slots/month to protect the release schedule.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns &#x27;occasional commissions&#x27; into a listed product line. 3 orders/mo × $350 avg = ~$1,050/mo at maybe 2 hours of human time per order; the turnaround SLA is itself the marketing hook.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — high-margin one-time revenue; anchors pricing for everything else</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Overnight autonomous 44-panel run (fulfillment engine), creator.php QA defect scan (revision pass), commission intake funnel (beyond)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="season compilation pdfs on gumroad + itch.io (one-time purchase line) package each completed season into a 100+ page &#x27;graphic novel&#x27; pdf (page-composer already exports print-ready pdf) with a new cover, and list at $12-20 on gumroad and itch.io&#x27;s adult section — reaching one-time buyers who will never subscribe, plus churned ex-patrons. start with complete growgetter vol. 1 and one maxx volume; add each new season on completion. itch.io&#x27;s adult-comics browse pages double as a discovery channel. at a modest 40 sales/mo across titles × $15 = ~$600/mo with zero new production. also monetizes churned patrons (win-back email: &#x27;own the season you missed&#x27;)."><summary><span class="t">Season compilation PDFs on Gumroad + itch.io (one-time purchase line)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Package each completed season into a 100+ page &#x27;graphic novel&#x27; PDF (page-composer already exports print-ready PDF) with a new cover, and list at $12-20 on Gumroad and itch.io&#x27;s adult section — reaching one-time buyers who will never subscribe, plus churned ex-patrons. Start with Complete GrowGetter Vol. 1 and one Maxx volume; add each new season on completion. itch.io&#x27;s adult-comics browse pages double as a discovery channel.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> At a modest 40 sales/mo across titles × $15 = ~$600/mo with zero new production. Also monetizes churned patrons (win-back email: &#x27;own the season you missed&#x27;).</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — one-time sales to non-subscribers and churned patrons</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> page-composer PDF export, pdf skill; distinct from the excluded Vault tier (subscription access) — these are one-time purchase products on external storefronts</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="seasonal specials calendar (4-6 annual one-shot events) pre-plan an annual calendar — summer beach special (the baywatch cast is literally ready), halloween transformation special, anniversary special, holiday special — each a 10-15 page one-shot produced in a single overnight run from a pre-approved premise. lock the calendar once; each special auto-schedules its production job 2 weeks ahead. specials release simultaneously across all 4 accounts as shared &#x27;event&#x27; content. event content measurably suppresses cancel-timing (&#x27;stay for the halloween special&#x27;) and gives alternate ready-made social moments. cost is ~4 overnight runs/year; retention effect on even 10 would-cancel patrons per event × $5 ≈ $200-300/yr per event plus engagement halo."><summary><span class="t">Seasonal specials calendar (4-6 annual one-shot events)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Pre-plan an annual calendar — Summer Beach Special (the Baywatch cast is literally ready), Halloween transformation special, anniversary special, holiday special — each a 10-15 page one-shot produced in a single overnight run from a pre-approved premise. Lock the calendar once; each special auto-schedules its production job 2 weeks ahead. Specials release simultaneously across all 4 accounts as shared &#x27;event&#x27; content.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Event content measurably suppresses cancel-timing (&#x27;stay for the Halloween special&#x27;) and gives Alternate ready-made social moments. Cost is ~4 overnight runs/year; retention effect on even 10 would-cancel patrons per event × $5 ≈ $200-300/yr per event plus engagement halo.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention — cancel-suppression around dated events; cross-account engagement spikes</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Baywatch cast outfit locks (Lana/Lacy), overnight run, scheduled-tasks for auto-queued production jobs</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="director&#x27;s cut extended editions: inject new growth pages into fan-favorite chapters the corpus findings say growth density is the product — apply that ruler to the back catalog: identify the 10 most-loved chapters with the lowest growth-panel ratio, and produce +3-5 new multi-panel growth-sequence pages per chapter (refs, wardrobe locks, and continuity are all known quantities, so these are the cheapest possible pages to generate). release as &#x27;extended edition&#x27; drops on off-weeks and bundle them into the compilation pdfs as an upsell differentiator. new releases from existing ip at maybe 20% the cost of a fresh chapter. fills 10 off-week release slots; &#x27;extended&#x27; versions also justify a $3-5 price bump on compilation pdfs."><summary><span class="t">Director&#x27;s Cut extended editions: inject new growth pages into fan-favorite chapters</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention + ARPU</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The corpus findings say growth density is the product — apply that ruler to the back catalog: identify the 10 most-loved chapters with the lowest growth-panel ratio, and produce +3-5 NEW multi-panel growth-sequence pages per chapter (refs, wardrobe locks, and continuity are all known quantities, so these are the cheapest possible pages to generate). Release as &#x27;Extended Edition&#x27; drops on off-weeks and bundle them into the compilation PDFs as an upsell differentiator.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> New releases from existing IP at maybe 20% the cost of a fresh chapter. Fills 10 off-week release slots; &#x27;Extended&#x27; versions also justify a $3-5 price bump on compilation PDFs.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention + ARPU — more release slots filled cheaply; premium-izes compilations</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comic-corpus growth-ratio findings, growth density mandate, continuity-check, existing character locks</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="S" data-hor="days" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="character spin-off mini line: 4-6 page shorts starring proven fan favorites mira, the baywatch duo, and other locked-cast favorites get standalone 4-6 page mini-stories slotted between main releases. since refs, size guides, and wardrobe locks already exist, a mini is a half-night production job. use patreon comment/like data (via creator pulse) to pick which character gets the next mini; brand it as a recurring &#x27;spotlight&#x27; series so it reads as a feature, not filler. doubles perceived release frequency on the flagship for ~30% of the production cost of full chapters. more touches per month is a direct churn suppressant, and spotlight polls give patrons a participation hook."><summary><span class="t">Character spin-off mini line: 4-6 page shorts starring proven fan favorites</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">days</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Mira, the Baywatch duo, and other locked-cast favorites get standalone 4-6 page mini-stories slotted between main releases. Since refs, size guides, and wardrobe locks already exist, a mini is a half-night production job. Use Patreon comment/like data (via Creator Pulse) to pick which character gets the next mini; brand it as a recurring &#x27;Spotlight&#x27; series so it reads as a feature, not filler.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Doubles perceived release frequency on the flagship for ~30% of the production cost of full chapters. More touches per month is a direct churn suppressant, and Spotlight polls give patrons a participation hook.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention — higher touch frequency between flagship releases</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Mira character anchor, Baywatch cast locks, Creator Pulse engagement data for character selection</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="L" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="live branching chapters: mid-story growth-path votes produced within 48 hours goes beyond the excluded monthly story polls (premise selection): this is mid-story interactivity only ai production speed makes possible. a chapter releases to a cliffhanger with a 2-option vote (&#x27;she drains the whole vial / half&#x27;); the top tier votes for 24h, and the winning branch is produced overnight and drops 48h later. run it as a quarterly event on growgetter first; the losing branch can later ship as a &#x27;what if&#x27; bonus, so no generation is wasted. no human-artist competitor can offer vote-to-page in 48 hours — it is a subscription hook unique to this pipeline. gate voting at a +$2-3 tier: at 300 patrons with 20% opting in, ~$150/mo arpu plus a strong stay-subscribed reason during events."><summary><span class="t">Live branching chapters: mid-story growth-path votes produced within 48 hours</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU + retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the excluded monthly story polls (premise selection): this is mid-story interactivity only AI production speed makes possible. A chapter releases to a cliffhanger with a 2-option vote (&#x27;she drains the whole vial / half&#x27;); the top tier votes for 24h, and the winning branch is produced overnight and drops 48h later. Run it as a quarterly event on GrowGetter first; the losing branch can later ship as a &#x27;What If&#x27; bonus, so no generation is wasted.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> No human-artist competitor can offer vote-to-page in 48 hours — it is a subscription hook unique to this pipeline. Gate voting at a +$2-3 tier: at 300 patrons with 20% opting in, ~$150/mo ARPU plus a strong stay-subscribed reason during events.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU + retention — paid voting tier; event mechanics suppress cancels</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Monthly patron story polls (beyond), overnight runner, script-breakdown for pre-planned branch shotlists</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="daily &#x27;growth shots&#x27; single-page line as the top-of-funnel firehose beyond the growgetter.php random-comic tool (an internal toy): make one-page, self-contained sfw growth gags a public-facing daily content line under the musclegrowthai brand — one page, one growth beat, one punchline, posted daily to deviantart (and twitter/ig when live), each carrying a property plug. the generator + qa defect scan already exist; add a genspec template and a 30-day approved queue the owner reviews in one weekly sitting (posting itself stays human-approved per the posting rule). daily presence in da feeds at ~zero marginal cost is how the niche&#x27;s biggest accounts grew. 30 posts/mo × modest da reach compounding into even 10-15 new patrons/mo at $5 is $50-75/mo of new compounding mrr, plus watcher growth as a hedge on patreon platform risk."><summary><span class="t">Daily &#x27;Growth Shots&#x27; single-page line as the top-of-funnel firehose</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Beyond the growgetter.php random-comic tool (an internal toy): make one-page, self-contained SFW growth gags a public-facing daily content line under the MuscleGrowthAI brand — one page, one growth beat, one punchline, posted daily to DeviantArt (and Twitter/IG when live), each carrying a property plug. The generator + QA defect scan already exist; add a genspec template and a 30-day approved queue the owner reviews in one weekly sitting (posting itself stays human-approved per the posting rule).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Daily presence in DA feeds at ~zero marginal cost is how the niche&#x27;s biggest accounts grew. 30 posts/mo × modest DA reach compounding into even 10-15 new patrons/mo at $5 is $50-75/mo of new compounding MRR, plus watcher growth as a hedge on Patreon platform risk.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion — daily discovery surface feeding all properties&#x27; funnels</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> growgetter.php random-comic generator (beyond), ck_ai_qa defect scan, never-post-without-permission rule (owner batch-approves weekly)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="scale" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="print-on-demand physical editions via lulu/kdp + limited signed runs page-composer already exports print-ready pdf — push completed season compilations to lulu (explicit-friendly) as $30-40 trade paperbacks, and run one numbered &#x27;limited edition&#x27; print run per year as the top-patreon-tier annual reward. phase: format check + one proof copy first, then list two volumes, then wire &#x27;annual print book&#x27; into the top tier&#x27;s benefits copy. small but very high-signal: 10-15 books/mo × ~$12 margin ≈ $150/mo, and the annual print reward materially strengthens the top tier&#x27;s retention story (physical artifacts are the stickiest perk class on patreon)."><summary><span class="t">Print-on-demand physical editions via Lulu/KDP + limited signed runs</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Scale-Up</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:owner</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream + retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>page-composer already exports print-ready PDF — push completed season compilations to Lulu (explicit-friendly) as $30-40 trade paperbacks, and run one numbered &#x27;limited edition&#x27; print run per year as the top-Patreon-tier annual reward. Phase: format check + one proof copy first, then list two volumes, then wire &#x27;annual print book&#x27; into the top tier&#x27;s benefits copy.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Small but very high-signal: 10-15 books/mo × ~$12 margin ≈ $150/mo, and the annual print reward materially strengthens the top tier&#x27;s retention story (physical artifacts are the stickiest perk class on Patreon).</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream + retention — physical margin plus a top-tier anchor perk</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> page-composer print-ready PDF export, season compilation masters from the Gumroad line</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="moonshots"><h3>Moonshots <span class="n">15</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="&quot;choose your growth&quot; — branching interactive comic engine on the custom site build a branching-reader layer into 3dmusclecomics.com: a json story-graph format (nodes = pages, edges = choices) extending the comics.js manifest, a choice ui at page bottom, and localstorage path tracking. phase 1 (wk 1-2): reader engine + one 3-branch growgetter side story authored largely from existing alternate/trashed panel takes. phase 2 (wk 3-4): extend the script-breakdown skill to emit per-branch shotlists and generate the deltas via bridge.php worker jobs. phase 3: patreon-gate premium branches (free readers walk one path, patrons unlock all) plus a monthly vote-to-canonize-the-path event. a format no one else in the muscle-growth niche ships. at 500 patrons, a $3 all-paths upsell taken by 20% = +$300/mo, and vote-to-canonize gives lapsed patrons a recurring reason to come back each month."><summary><span class="t">&quot;Choose Your Growth&quot; — branching interactive comic engine on the custom site</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU (path-unlock upsell) + </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Build a branching-reader layer into 3dmusclecomics.com: a JSON story-graph format (nodes = pages, edges = choices) extending the comics.js manifest, a choice UI at page bottom, and localStorage path tracking. Phase 1 (wk 1-2): reader engine + one 3-branch GrowGetter side story authored largely from existing alternate/trashed panel takes. Phase 2 (wk 3-4): extend the script-breakdown skill to emit per-branch shotlists and generate the deltas via bridge.php worker jobs. Phase 3: Patreon-gate premium branches (free readers walk one path, patrons unlock all) plus a monthly vote-to-canonize-the-path event.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> A format no one else in the muscle-growth niche ships. At 500 patrons, a $3 all-paths upsell taken by 20% = +$300/mo, and vote-to-canonize gives lapsed patrons a recurring reason to come back each month.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU (path-unlock upsell) + retention (monthly canon votes)</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest, script-breakdown skill, bridge.php worker protocol</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="&quot;your growth story&quot; — personalized oc mini-comic top tier a capped top patreon tier ($75-100/mo, 10-15 seats): the patron submits an original character via a structured intake form (description + growth-flavor/intensity preference sliders) and receives a private 6-10 page mini-comic monthly. phase 1: studio intake form + character-lock generator reusing the cast-lineup/character-lock lessons; run a paid pilot with 2 volunteer patrons. phase 2: productionize as a bridge.php job kind behind the comic-production qa gate chain, with gwhar reviewing scripts pre-generation. phase 3: open publicly with a waitlist above cap and raise price on demand. 10 seats × $85 = +$850/mo, and the marginal cost is roughly one proven overnight autonomous run per patron. churn on this tier should be near zero — cancelling means abandoning their own character mid-story."><summary><span class="t">&quot;Your Growth Story&quot; — personalized OC mini-comic top tier</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A capped top Patreon tier ($75-100/mo, 10-15 seats): the patron submits an original character via a structured intake form (description + growth-flavor/intensity preference sliders) and receives a private 6-10 page mini-comic monthly. Phase 1: studio intake form + character-lock generator reusing the cast-lineup/character-lock lessons; run a paid pilot with 2 volunteer patrons. Phase 2: productionize as a bridge.php job kind behind the comic-production QA gate chain, with GWHAR reviewing scripts pre-generation. Phase 3: open publicly with a waitlist above cap and raise price on demand.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> 10 seats × $85 = +$850/mo, and the marginal cost is roughly one proven overnight autonomous run per patron. Churn on this tier should be near zero — cancelling means abandoning their own character mid-story.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — high-price capped tier with structurally low churn</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Proven 44-panel overnight autonomous run, character-lock/cast-lineup lessons, bridge.php genspec, QA gate chain</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="growgetter animated — a real seedance season for youtube + patreon scale the proven müller-02 pipeline (47 panels → 18 clips) into a 6-8 episode season of 3-5 minute episodes built from back-catalog chapters. phase 1 (wk 1-2): episode template — shotlist → seedance mini iteration → std finals, ai voice pass, music bed, ffmpeg assembly; ship episode 1. phase 2 (wk 3-6): batch 3+ more episodes via overnight worker runs; alternate handles the youtube channel and uploads (each with per-post approval). phase 3: patreon early-access window (2-4 weeks before youtube) with end-card ctas pointing back to patreon. muscle-growth animation clips routinely clear 100k views on youtube; even 50k views/ep at 0.5% click-through = 250 patreon visits per episode, and an early-access window is one of the strongest documented churn reducers on patreon."><summary><span class="t">GrowGetter Animated — a real Seedance season for YouTube + Patreon</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion (YouTube top-of-f</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Scale the proven Müller-02 pipeline (47 panels → 18 clips) into a 6-8 episode season of 3-5 minute episodes built from back-catalog chapters. Phase 1 (wk 1-2): episode template — shotlist → Seedance mini iteration → std finals, AI voice pass, music bed, ffmpeg assembly; ship Episode 1. Phase 2 (wk 3-6): batch 3+ more episodes via overnight worker runs; Alternate handles the YouTube channel and uploads (each with per-post approval). Phase 3: Patreon early-access window (2-4 weeks before YouTube) with end-card CTAs pointing back to Patreon.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Muscle-growth animation clips routinely clear 100k views on YouTube; even 50k views/ep at 0.5% click-through = 250 Patreon visits per episode, and an early-access window is one of the strongest documented churn reducers on Patreon.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion (YouTube top-of-funnel) + retention (early-access window)</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Seedance video pipeline, Müller-02 shotlist template, studio worker protocol; goes far beyond the excluded per-release auto-trailer</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="3dmc reader — installable pwa with offline chapters and release-day push wrap the static site&#x27;s reader in a pwa: manifest.json + service worker for offline chapter caching, install prompt, and web push for new releases. phase 1: installable shell + offline caching using comics.js as the catalog api. phase 2: push notifications triggered automatically when a new comics.js entry lands, plus reading-position sync. phase 3: patron login deep-links so gated chapters open in-app, making the app — not patreon&#x27;s feed — the daily habit surface. push is the cheapest churn lever available — release-day push typically drives 3-10x the return rate of email — and it builds an owned notification channel that survives any patreon feed or policy change."><summary><span class="t">3DMC Reader — installable PWA with offline chapters and release-day push</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Wrap the static site&#x27;s reader in a PWA: manifest.json + service worker for offline chapter caching, install prompt, and Web Push for new releases. Phase 1: installable shell + offline caching using comics.js as the catalog API. Phase 2: push notifications triggered automatically when a new comics.js entry lands, plus reading-position sync. Phase 3: patron login deep-links so gated chapters open in-app, making the app — not Patreon&#x27;s feed — the daily habit surface.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Push is the cheapest churn lever available — release-day push typically drives 3-10x the return rate of email — and it builds an owned notification channel that survives any Patreon feed or policy change.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention — owned re-engagement channel raises release-day return rate</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest, feed.xml release flow, studio PHP session layer</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="ghost studio — sell the pipeline to other creators for rev-share offer the full production line (script-breakdown → generation → qa gates → lettering) to 2-3 other adult-comic creators at $30-60/page or 30-50% rev-share. phase 1 (wk 1-3): make the pipeline multi-tenant — per-client cast locks, style locks, separate studio output buckets — and produce one free pilot chapter for a mid-size da/patreon creator as the case study. phase 2 (wk 4-8): pricing sheet, simple contract, and a client-facing proof page (approve/reject panels without studio access). phase 3: three paying clients, with gwhar scouting candidates — he already loves reading across the niche. one 20-page chapter/month per client at $40/page = $800/client/mo; 3 clients = +$2,400/mo — plausibly the largest single new stream, and every future pipeline improvement gets amortized across paying customers."><summary><span class="t">Ghost Studio — sell the pipeline to other creators for rev-share</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Offer the full production line (script-breakdown → generation → QA gates → lettering) to 2-3 other adult-comic creators at $30-60/page or 30-50% rev-share. Phase 1 (wk 1-3): make the pipeline multi-tenant — per-client cast locks, style locks, separate studio output buckets — and produce one free pilot chapter for a mid-size DA/Patreon creator as the case study. Phase 2 (wk 4-8): pricing sheet, simple contract, and a client-facing proof page (approve/reject panels without studio access). Phase 3: three paying clients, with GWHAR scouting candidates — he already loves reading across the niche.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> One 20-page chapter/month per client at $40/page = $800/client/mo; 3 clients = +$2,400/mo — plausibly the largest single new stream, and every future pipeline improvement gets amortized across paying customers.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — production-as-a-service fees / rev-share</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> claude-comic-pipeline (35 lessons + QA gate chain), studio worker protocol, GWHAR&#x27;s story-scout role</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="talk to the cast — in-universe ai companion premium add-on a $10-15/mo add-on: patrons chat with canon characters (growgetter leads, lana/lacy, mira) via a gated web chat on the studio php stack or a discord bot, powered by the claude api with persona cards distilled from the existing character-lock docs plus strict content guardrails. phase 1: one character, 10 beta patrons. phase 2: persistent per-patron memory (their private canon survives between sessions) and weekly in-character check-in messages as the retention hook. phase 3: the bot teases upcoming chapters and can commission a one-panel &quot;gift&quot; image of the conversation through the worker protocol. 40 subscribers × $12 = +$480/mo against likely &lt;$50/mo api cost. parasocial products churn materially less than content tiers — cancelling deletes the relationship and the memory."><summary><span class="t">Talk to the Cast — in-universe AI companion premium add-on</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU add-on + retention via </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A $10-15/mo add-on: patrons chat with canon characters (GrowGetter leads, Lana/Lacy, Mira) via a gated web chat on the studio PHP stack or a Discord bot, powered by the Claude API with persona cards distilled from the existing character-lock docs plus strict content guardrails. Phase 1: one character, 10 beta patrons. Phase 2: persistent per-patron memory (their private canon survives between sessions) and weekly in-character check-in messages as the retention hook. Phase 3: the bot teases upcoming chapters and can commission a one-panel &quot;gift&quot; image of the conversation through the worker protocol.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> 40 subscribers × $12 = +$480/mo against likely &lt;$50/mo API cost. Parasocial products churn materially less than content tiers — cancelling deletes the relationship and the memory.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU add-on + retention via persistent per-patron memory</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Character-lock docs (Mira anchor, Baywatch cast lock, Vespers premise), bridge.php gift-image jobs, studio login</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="growgetter: the interview — visual novel on itch.io, then steam a ren&#x27;py visual novel assembled substantially from existing assets: back-catalog panels re-exported as cgs, sprites via the cast-lineup flow, branching script developed through the story-writers-room process. phase 1 (wk 1-3): a free 30-minute vertical slice on itch.io as a list-builder. phase 2 (wk 4-8): full 2-3 hour game, 3 routes, gallery unlock, $12-15. phase 3: steam release (adult vns pass review with correct tagging) plus a dev-log patreon tier for the game audience. niche adult vns commonly sell 500-2,000 units in year one; 800 units × $13 at itch&#x27;s ~90% cut ≈ $9.4k, and itch/steam is an acquisition channel completely outside the current patreon/da ceiling."><summary><span class="t">GrowGetter: The Interview — visual novel on itch.io, then Steam</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A Ren&#x27;Py visual novel assembled substantially from existing assets: back-catalog panels re-exported as CGs, sprites via the cast-lineup flow, branching script developed through the story-writers-room process. Phase 1 (wk 1-3): a free 30-minute vertical slice on itch.io as a list-builder. Phase 2 (wk 4-8): full 2-3 hour game, 3 routes, gallery unlock, $12-15. Phase 3: Steam release (adult VNs pass review with correct tagging) plus a dev-log Patreon tier for the game audience.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Niche adult VNs commonly sell 500-2,000 units in year one; 800 units × $13 at itch&#x27;s ~90% cut ≈ $9.4k, and itch/Steam is an acquisition channel completely outside the current Patreon/DA ceiling.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — one-off game sales + new acquisition channel</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Back-catalog panel archive, cast-lineup generation flow, story-writers-room skill</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="localized site mirrors (es/de/zh) — the distribution layer the translation conveyor lacks the prior wave proposed the translation conveyor (content production); this builds the missing surface: es./de./zh. subdomains of the static site. phase 1: a mirror generator that walks comics.js, emits per-locale manifests, translated ui strings, and hreflang tags; launch es first (largest untapped da demographic). phase 2: per-locale rss and landing pages, with attribution.php measuring which locale actually converts. phase 3: if es converts, roll de + zh and add a localized patreon welcome flow (translated tier copy and welcome posts). comparable adult-comic sites report 20-35% of traffic from es/de markets that currently bounces off english-only pages; converting even 5% of that segment is free growth, and hreflang mirrors compound via seo for months."><summary><span class="t">Localized site mirrors (es/de/zh) — the distribution layer the translation conveyor lacks</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The prior wave proposed the translation conveyor (content production); this builds the missing surface: es./de./zh. subdomains of the static site. Phase 1: a mirror generator that walks comics.js, emits per-locale manifests, translated UI strings, and hreflang tags; launch ES first (largest untapped DA demographic). Phase 2: per-locale RSS and landing pages, with attribution.php measuring which locale actually converts. Phase 3: if ES converts, roll DE + ZH and add a localized Patreon welcome flow (translated tier copy and welcome posts).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Comparable adult-comic sites report 20-35% of traffic from ES/DE markets that currently bounces off English-only pages; converting even 5% of that segment is free growth, and hreflang mirrors compound via SEO for months.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion — opens the non-English funnel end-to-end</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Translation conveyor (prior wave — this is its distribution layer, not a re-proposal), comics.js, attribution.php cockpit</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="3dmc prime — direct membership on the site (the patreon hedge) own subscription checkout on 3dmusclecomics.com with an adult-tolerant processor (ccbill/segpay; stripe only if staying sfw-side), gating chapters via the same php session layer the studio login already uses. phase 1 (wk 1-2): processor selection and compliance review — this is the real gate — then a single $10/mo plan with webhook → member table → gated reader. phase 2 (wk 3-6): make the pwa reader the member client, offer existing patrons $1-off grandfather pricing to migrate, add dunning emails. phase 3: keep patreon as acquisition top-of-funnel with direct as the destination, tracking migration in the attribution cockpit and creator pulse. recaptures patreon&#x27;s ~8% + payment fees immediately, but the real value is existential: all 4 patreon accounts can vanish in one policy sweep, and this makes the audience and revenue survivable. at $3k/mo with 30% migrated, fee recapture alone is ~$90/mo before any pricing freedom."><summary><span class="t">3DMC Prime — direct membership on the site (the Patreon hedge)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Margin (fee recapture) + ret</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Own subscription checkout on 3dmusclecomics.com with an adult-tolerant processor (CCBill/Segpay; Stripe only if staying SFW-side), gating chapters via the same PHP session layer the studio login already uses. Phase 1 (wk 1-2): processor selection and compliance review — this is the real gate — then a single $10/mo plan with webhook → member table → gated reader. Phase 2 (wk 3-6): make the PWA reader the member client, offer existing patrons $1-off grandfather pricing to migrate, add dunning emails. Phase 3: keep Patreon as acquisition top-of-funnel with direct as the destination, tracking migration in the attribution cockpit and Creator Pulse.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Recaptures Patreon&#x27;s ~8% + payment fees immediately, but the real value is existential: all 4 Patreon accounts can vanish in one policy sweep, and this makes the audience and revenue survivable. At $3k/mo with 30% migrated, fee recapture alone is ~$90/mo before any pricing freedom.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Margin (fee recapture) + retention insurance against platform risk</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Studio PHP login/session code, PWA reader project, Creator Pulse, attribution.php</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="collected-editions storefront — one-off volumes for the 90% who never subscribe package back-catalog chapters into collected volumes (pdf + cbz via page-composer&#x27;s print-ready export, plus overnight-generated exclusive pin-ups) sold one-off on itch.io/gumroad and embedded on-site. phase 1: growgetter vol. 1 (5 chapters + 10 exclusive pin-ups) at $15, announced across all 4 patreon audiences with per-post approval. phase 2: monthly cadence — each volume assembled by a worker job from the manifest, alternate handles store listings. phase 3: seasonal bundles and a $60-80 complete-works pack. one-off sales monetize the large majority of followers who never subscribe; niche creators typically see $500-1,500 per volume launch, nearly pure margin since the pages already exist. distinct mechanism from the excluded vault subscription tier — this is à-la-carte, off-patreon."><summary><span class="t">Collected-editions storefront — one-off volumes for the 90% who never subscribe</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Package back-catalog chapters into collected volumes (PDF + CBZ via page-composer&#x27;s print-ready export, plus overnight-generated exclusive pin-ups) sold one-off on itch.io/Gumroad and embedded on-site. Phase 1: GrowGetter Vol. 1 (5 chapters + 10 exclusive pin-ups) at $15, announced across all 4 Patreon audiences with per-post approval. Phase 2: monthly cadence — each volume assembled by a worker job from the manifest, Alternate handles store listings. Phase 3: seasonal bundles and a $60-80 complete-works pack.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> One-off sales monetize the large majority of followers who never subscribe; niche creators typically see $500-1,500 per volume launch, nearly pure margin since the pages already exist. Distinct mechanism from the excluded Vault subscription tier — this is à-la-carte, off-Patreon.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — one-off sales to non-subscribers</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> page-composer PDF export, comics.js back-catalog, overnight generation for bonus pages</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="self-serve commission engine — configurator to genspec to overnight run goes well beyond the previously-proposed intake funnel: a public configurator on the site (character type, growth flavor, page count, sfw/nsfw) that returns an instant quote ($150-400), takes a deposit, and compiles the order directly into a bridge.php genspec so fulfillment is a scheduled overnight run through the qa gate chain. phase 1: configurator with pricing calibrated from the per-chapter cost ledger; fulfill the first 3 orders manually to validate margins. phase 2: automatic genspec compilation plus a client proof-approval page. phase 3: capacity-based dynamic pricing and a monthly slot drop announced to patreon as a scarcity event. commissions today are occasional; a self-serve funnel at just 4 orders/mo × $250 average = +$1,000/mo, with the overnight run driving labor per order toward zero."><summary><span class="t">Self-serve commission engine — configurator to genspec to overnight run</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes well beyond the previously-proposed intake funnel: a public configurator on the site (character type, growth flavor, page count, SFW/NSFW) that returns an instant quote ($150-400), takes a deposit, and compiles the order directly into a bridge.php genspec so fulfillment is a scheduled overnight run through the QA gate chain. Phase 1: configurator with pricing calibrated from the per-chapter cost ledger; fulfill the first 3 orders manually to validate margins. Phase 2: automatic genspec compilation plus a client proof-approval page. Phase 3: capacity-based dynamic pricing and a monthly slot drop announced to Patreon as a scarcity event.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Commissions today are occasional; a self-serve funnel at just 4 orders/mo × $250 average = +$1,000/mo, with the overnight run driving labor per order toward zero.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — productized commissions at pipeline marginal cost</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php genspec protocol, proven overnight autonomous run, per-chapter cost ledger (prior wave); supersedes the excluded intake-funnel idea</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="own-model stack — character loras trained on the 8,840-gen archive hedge the flow/higgsfield dependency (filter roulette, pricing, model retirements — flash already died once) by training per-character loras on an open model (flux/sdxl) using the higgsfield archive, on rented gpu (~$0.50/hr runpod). phase 1 (wk 1-2): export and caption the top ~200 archive images per flagship character, train a growgetter-lead lora, benchmark against nb pro using the canonical qa rubric. phase 2 (wk 3-6): on parity, expose a comfyui endpoint as a new backend behind bridge.php so workers route jobs per-panel. phase 3: per-oc lora training — the enabling tech for the personalized-comic tier at scale — with zero nsfw-filter tax. kills the 4x-retry nsfw filter tax and per-image fees on the highest-volume panels, and de-risks the entire operation from a single vendor pulling the plug. its biggest payoff is unlocking the $850+/mo personalized tier at scale."><summary><span class="t">Own-model stack — character LoRAs trained on the 8,840-gen archive</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Margin (no filter/per-image </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Hedge the Flow/Higgsfield dependency (filter roulette, pricing, model retirements — flash already died once) by training per-character LoRAs on an open model (Flux/SDXL) using the Higgsfield archive, on rented GPU (~$0.50/hr RunPod). Phase 1 (wk 1-2): export and caption the top ~200 archive images per flagship character, train a GrowGetter-lead LoRA, benchmark against NB Pro using the canonical QA rubric. Phase 2 (wk 3-6): on parity, expose a ComfyUI endpoint as a new backend behind bridge.php so workers route jobs per-panel. Phase 3: per-OC LoRA training — the enabling tech for the personalized-comic tier at scale — with zero NSFW-filter tax.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Kills the 4x-retry NSFW filter tax and per-image fees on the highest-volume panels, and de-risks the entire operation from a single vendor pulling the plug. Its biggest payoff is unlocking the $850+/mo personalized tier at scale.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Margin (no filter/per-image tax) + enabler for the high-ARPU personalized tier</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Higgsfield archive (8,840 gens via show_generations), canonical QA rubric, bridge.php backend abstraction</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="launch 3dgiantesscomics as a real second brand the scaffold exists and sits undeployed — giantess/growth is an adjacent kink with a large paying audience that barely overlaps muscle-growth. phase 1 (wk 1-2): deploy the scaffold via its sandboxed deploy.sh, pick a flagship premise through the writers-room process, produce chapters 1-2 on the standard pipeline. phase 2 (wk 3-6): dedicated patreon + da accounts and an 8-chapter runway built by overnight runs; creator pulse adds it as account 5. phase 3: one cross-promo to the muscle audience, then let it grow on its own da/seo legs. reruns the entire proven playbook against a fresh market on tooling that is already paid for; reaching even 25% of the main operation&#x27;s patreon in year one is a mid-hundreds-per-month stream, and it diversifies platform and niche risk simultaneously."><summary><span class="t">Launch 3dgiantesscomics as a real second brand</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The scaffold exists and sits undeployed — giantess/growth is an adjacent kink with a large paying audience that barely overlaps muscle-growth. Phase 1 (wk 1-2): deploy the scaffold via its sandboxed deploy.sh, pick a flagship premise through the writers-room process, produce chapters 1-2 on the standard pipeline. Phase 2 (wk 3-6): dedicated Patreon + DA accounts and an 8-chapter runway built by overnight runs; Creator Pulse adds it as account 5. Phase 3: one cross-promo to the muscle audience, then let it grow on its own DA/SEO legs.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Reruns the entire proven playbook against a fresh market on tooling that is already paid for; reaching even 25% of the main operation&#x27;s Patreon in year one is a mid-hundreds-per-month stream, and it diversifies platform and niche risk simultaneously.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — second vertical on amortized tooling</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> 3dgiantesscomics scaffold (built, undeployed), full comic pipeline, Creator Pulse rollup</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="growgetter: year one — crowdfunded print omnibus a 30-day kickstarter/backerkit campaign for a 150-200 page printed omnibus with tiered rewards: pdf $15, softcover $35, hardcover + custom pin-up of the backer&#x27;s chosen character $95. phase 1 (wk 1-3): print-ready remaster via the page-composer pdf pipeline plus an upscaling pass; quote pod (mixam/kablam) vs offset. phase 2 (wk 4-6): campaign page and a seedance-built trailer, promoted across all 4 patreons + da with per-post approval. phase 3: pod fulfillment (no inventory risk); custom pin-up rewards run as overnight worker jobs. niche comic kickstarters routinely fund $5-20k; a conservative 150 backers × $45 average = $6.75k gross, and a campaign is a proven reactivation event for lapsed patrons who want the physical artifact."><summary><span class="t">GrowGetter: Year One — crowdfunded print omnibus</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A 30-day Kickstarter/BackerKit campaign for a 150-200 page printed omnibus with tiered rewards: PDF $15, softcover $35, hardcover + custom pin-up of the backer&#x27;s chosen character $95. Phase 1 (wk 1-3): print-ready remaster via the page-composer PDF pipeline plus an upscaling pass; quote POD (Mixam/KaBlam) vs offset. Phase 2 (wk 4-6): campaign page and a Seedance-built trailer, promoted across all 4 Patreons + DA with per-post approval. Phase 3: POD fulfillment (no inventory risk); custom pin-up rewards run as overnight worker jobs.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Niche comic Kickstarters routinely fund $5-20k; a conservative 150 backers × $45 average = $6.75k gross, and a campaign is a proven reactivation event for lapsed patrons who want the physical artifact.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream — one-time crowdfund + lapsed-patron reactivation halo</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> page-composer print export, upscale pipeline, Seedance trailer capability, overnight runs for backer pin-ups</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="moonshots" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="motion-comic dub channel — the volume youtube play (distinct from full animation) deliberately different cost point from the seedance season: motion comics are ~10x cheaper per minute — existing pages, ken burns pan/zoom in ffmpeg, ai voice per speech bubble, sfx/music — enabling 2-3 narrated 5-8 minute episodes per week almost fully autonomously. phase 1: template the pipeline (page → panel crops reusing import.php&#x27;s snip logic → timed pans → tts → mix) and ship 3 episodes. phase 2: a worker job kind so every published chapter auto-produces its motion-comic 2 weeks after patreon release; alternate uploads on schedule with approval. phase 3: monetize the channel itself (ads on sfw cuts) and later feed localized dubs from the translation conveyor. volume beats polish for youtube discovery: 100+ searchable episodes/year vs 6-8 animated ones. comparable comic-dub channels reach 10-50k subs; channel ad revenue plus funnel traffic is additive to the animated season, not competitive with it."><summary><span class="t">Motion-comic dub channel — the volume YouTube play (distinct from full animation)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Moonshots</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream (YT ads) + evergr</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Deliberately different cost point from the Seedance season: motion comics are ~10x cheaper per minute — existing pages, Ken Burns pan/zoom in ffmpeg, AI voice per speech bubble, SFX/music — enabling 2-3 narrated 5-8 minute episodes per week almost fully autonomously. Phase 1: template the pipeline (page → panel crops reusing import.php&#x27;s snip logic → timed pans → TTS → mix) and ship 3 episodes. Phase 2: a worker job kind so every published chapter auto-produces its motion-comic 2 weeks after Patreon release; Alternate uploads on schedule with approval. Phase 3: monetize the channel itself (ads on SFW cuts) and later feed localized dubs from the translation conveyor.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Volume beats polish for YouTube discovery: 100+ searchable episodes/year vs 6-8 animated ones. Comparable comic-dub channels reach 10-50k subs; channel ad revenue plus funnel traffic is additive to the animated season, not competitive with it.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream (YT ads) + evergreen top-of-funnel conversion</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> import.php panel-snip logic, ffmpeg tooling from the Seedance QA workflow, translation conveyor for future dubs; beyond the excluded auto-trailer (full episodes, standing cadence)</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="fleet"><h3>Agent Fleet <span class="n">16</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="pulse strategist agent (weekly analytics-to-action memos) a weekly agent that reads the creator pulse 4-account rollup plus attribution.php funnel data, computes deltas (net patrons, pledge value, churn, traffic-source conversion), and writes a one-page strategy memo ending in exactly 3 concrete moves. each move is auto-filed as an ops.php task with aitag/aiplan and ownertype pre-set, so the recommendation lands directly in the existing triage workflow instead of dying in a doc. memos accumulate in a /studio/memos/ archive so month-over-month reasoning is auditable. turns already-collected pulse data into decisions the owner currently has no time to extract. even one caught trend per month (e.g. a tier bleeding patrons post-price-anchor) plausibly protects 2-5% of mrr."><summary><span class="t">Pulse Strategist Agent (weekly analytics-to-action memos)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion + retention: conv</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly agent that reads the Creator Pulse 4-account rollup plus attribution.php funnel data, computes deltas (net patrons, pledge value, churn, traffic-source conversion), and writes a one-page strategy memo ending in exactly 3 concrete moves. Each move is auto-filed as an ops.php task with aiTag/aiPlan and ownerType pre-set, so the recommendation lands directly in the existing triage workflow instead of dying in a doc. Memos accumulate in a /studio/memos/ archive so month-over-month reasoning is auditable.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns already-collected Pulse data into decisions the owner currently has no time to extract. Even one caught trend per month (e.g. a tier bleeding patrons post-price-anchor) plausibly protects 2-5% of MRR.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion + retention: converts passive analytics into weekly revenue interventions.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse daily sync, attribution.php cockpit, ops.php aiTag/aiPlan fields</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="pricing &amp; tier architect agent (per-account price-test program) a flagship agent that owns pricing across all 4 patreon accounts. phase 1 (weeks 1-2): instrument — pull pledge histograms, churn-by-tier, and tenure curves from pulse per account. phase 2 (weeks 3-4): propose — for each account, a tier-restructure brief (price points, perk ladder, grandfathering plan) presented as multiple-choice options per the owner&#x27;s high-stakes-poll preference. phase 3 (month 2+): run one owner-approved change per account per quarter, then publish a pre/post readout memo and feed the winner into the next account&#x27;s proposal. the agent never touches patreon settings itself — it produces exact click-by-click change instructions for the owner or alternate. arpu is the highest-leverage untouched dial. at 500 patrons across accounts, a $1.50 average pledge lift from tier restructuring is ~$9,000/yr; even a partial win on one account likely exceeds the whole gwhar budget."><summary><span class="t">Pricing &amp; Tier Architect Agent (per-account price-test program)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU: systematic price/tier </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A flagship agent that owns pricing across all 4 Patreon accounts. Phase 1 (weeks 1-2): instrument — pull pledge histograms, churn-by-tier, and tenure curves from Pulse per account. Phase 2 (weeks 3-4): propose — for each account, a tier-restructure brief (price points, perk ladder, grandfathering plan) presented as multiple-choice options per the owner&#x27;s high-stakes-poll preference. Phase 3 (month 2+): run one owner-approved change per account per quarter, then publish a pre/post readout memo and feed the winner into the next account&#x27;s proposal. The agent never touches Patreon settings itself — it produces exact click-by-click change instructions for the owner or Alternate.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> ARPU is the highest-leverage untouched dial. At 500 patrons across accounts, a $1.50 average pledge lift from tier restructuring is ~$9,000/yr; even a partial win on one account likely exceeds the whole GWHAR budget.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU: systematic price/tier optimization per property instead of never-revisited launch pricing.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse rollup, poll-on-high-stakes decision pattern, ops.php task filing</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="discord community-manager agent (reply drafting + sentiment desk) distinct from the already-proposed discord notifier/autopost (those push outward; this manages inbound conversation). a daily agent reads new discord messages via a bot token, drafts on-voice replies into an approval queue (never posts — per the standing no-post rule), tags superfans and at-risk grumbling, and answers routine questions (release etas, where-to-find-chapter) from a maintained faq file. weekly it emits a sentiment digest: hottest threads, unanswered questions older than 48h, and members whose activity dropped. discord is the only owned community channel (patreon owns the rest); response latency dropping from days to hours is a direct retention lever. community-engaged patrons plausibly churn 20-30% less, worth ~$100-300/mo at typical scale."><summary><span class="t">Discord Community-Manager Agent (reply drafting + sentiment desk)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention: faster, consisten</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Distinct from the already-proposed Discord notifier/autopost (those push outward; this manages inbound conversation). A daily agent reads new Discord messages via a bot token, drafts on-voice replies into an approval queue (never posts — per the standing no-post rule), tags superfans and at-risk grumbling, and answers routine questions (release ETAs, where-to-find-chapter) from a maintained FAQ file. Weekly it emits a sentiment digest: hottest threads, unanswered questions older than 48h, and members whose activity dropped.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Discord is the only owned community channel (Patreon owns the rest); response latency dropping from days to hours is a direct retention lever. Community-engaged patrons plausibly churn 20-30% less, worth ~$100-300/mo at typical scale.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention: faster, consistent community response on the one platform-risk-free channel.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Never-post-without-permission rule as the approval gate; ops.php for escalations</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="competitive-intel agent (rival release radar) a weekly agent that crawls the public deviantart pages, patreon public tiers, and posted previews of a named watchlist of 10-15 rival muscle-growth/giantess creators. it logs release cadence, page counts, pricing, tier perks, and visible engagement (favorites/comments) into a structured intel file, and monthly writes a &#x27;what is working in the niche&#x27; diff memo: who raised prices, who launched video, which premise archetypes are getting outsized engagement. findings route as premise leads to gwhar&#x27;s story-scout lane and as pricing evidence to the pricing architect agent. the owner currently flies blind on the niche market. one adopted rival tactic per quarter (e.g. a proven perk structure or premise trend) plausibly moves conversion a few percent; also de-risks pricing decisions with real comps."><summary><span class="t">Competitive-Intel Agent (rival release radar)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion + ARPU: pricing c</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly agent that crawls the public DeviantArt pages, Patreon public tiers, and posted previews of a named watchlist of 10-15 rival muscle-growth/giantess creators. It logs release cadence, page counts, pricing, tier perks, and visible engagement (favorites/comments) into a structured intel file, and monthly writes a &#x27;what is working in the niche&#x27; diff memo: who raised prices, who launched video, which premise archetypes are getting outsized engagement. Findings route as premise leads to GWHAR&#x27;s story-scout lane and as pricing evidence to the Pricing Architect agent.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The owner currently flies blind on the niche market. One adopted rival tactic per quarter (e.g. a proven perk structure or premise trend) plausibly moves conversion a few percent; also de-risks pricing decisions with real comps.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion + ARPU: pricing comps and proven-perk evidence feed the pricing program.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> GWHAR story-scout intake lane (as a destination for premise leads), ops.php</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="seo custodian agent (ongoing site librarian, beyond the one-shot sitemap/json-ld idea) goes beyond the already-proposed one-time crawlable-transcript/sitemap work: this is a standing custodian. weekly it crawls 3dmusclecomics.com, diffs the comics.js manifest against live pages, checks feed.xml validity, broken links, missing meta/og tags, and page-speed regressions, and opens fix tasks or drafts patches deployed only via tools/deploy_3dmc.sh after approval. monthly it mines search console queries and drafts 1-2 new landing pages targeting search intent (character names, &#x27;muscle growth comic&#x27; long-tails) as sfw funnel entrances with utm-tagged patreon ctas. organic search is the only free, compounding acquisition channel the operation has. a custodian that keeps the funnel unbroken and adds 1-2 intent pages/month plausibly grows organic patreon referrals 10-20% over two quarters, measurable in attribution.php."><summary><span class="t">SEO Custodian Agent (ongoing site librarian, beyond the one-shot sitemap/JSON-LD idea)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion: compounding free</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the already-proposed one-time crawlable-transcript/sitemap work: this is a standing custodian. Weekly it crawls 3dmusclecomics.com, diffs the comics.js manifest against live pages, checks feed.xml validity, broken links, missing meta/OG tags, and page-speed regressions, and opens fix tasks or drafts patches deployed only via tools/deploy_3dmc.sh after approval. Monthly it mines Search Console queries and drafts 1-2 new landing pages targeting search intent (character names, &#x27;muscle growth comic&#x27; long-tails) as SFW funnel entrances with UTM-tagged Patreon CTAs.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Organic search is the only free, compounding acquisition channel the operation has. A custodian that keeps the funnel unbroken and adds 1-2 intent pages/month plausibly grows organic Patreon referrals 10-20% over two quarters, measurable in attribution.php.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion: compounding free top-of-funnel into the Patreon accounts.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest, feed.xml, attribution.php UTM tracking, deploy_3dmc.sh guardrail</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="qa librarian agent (defect telemetry → new codified lessons) a weekly agent that mines creator.php ck_ai_qa defect flags plus keep/trash decisions, clusters recurring failure modes (e.g. duplicate extras, wardrobe drift, dead-face), and checks each cluster against the existing 35 lessons in claude-comic-pipeline. where a cluster has no covering lesson, it drafts a new numbered lesson (l36+) with example panel evidence and a proposed prompt-level fix, submitted as a repo pr with a dated changelog entry per house rules. quarterly it also proposes retiring lessons whose defect class has vanished, keeping the rulebook lean. every codified lesson historically cut a whole defect class; automating lesson discovery raises first-pass keep-rate. at current volumes, a 10% keep-rate improvement is meaningful higgsfield credit savings plus faster chapter throughput."><summary><span class="t">QA Librarian Agent (defect telemetry → new codified lessons)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Margin: fewer paid re-genera</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly agent that mines creator.php ck_ai_qa defect flags plus keep/trash decisions, clusters recurring failure modes (e.g. duplicate extras, wardrobe drift, dead-face), and checks each cluster against the existing 35 lessons in claude-comic-pipeline. Where a cluster has no covering lesson, it drafts a new numbered lesson (L36+) with example panel evidence and a proposed prompt-level fix, submitted as a repo PR with a dated CHANGELOG entry per house rules. Quarterly it also proposes retiring lessons whose defect class has vanished, keeping the rulebook lean.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Every codified lesson historically cut a whole defect class; automating lesson discovery raises first-pass keep-rate. At current volumes, a 10% keep-rate improvement is meaningful Higgsfield credit savings plus faster chapter throughput.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Margin: fewer paid re-generations per shipped page; faster releases support cadence-driven retention.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> creator.php ck_ai_qa scan, keep/trash telemetry data, claude-comic-pipeline 35-lesson corpus, changelog rule</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="owner decision-capture agent (recurring sop scribe, beyond the one-time magna brain-dump) goes beyond the already-proposed one-time magna exit brain-dump: a recurring 15-minute weekly interview agent that asks the owner about decisions made that week (&#x27;why did you pick flow over higgsfield for that chapter?&#x27;, &#x27;what made that cover work?&#x27;), then writes or updates sop documents in a /sops/ directory of the pipeline repo. each sop is tagged by role (gwhar / alternate / ai-agent) so other fleet agents and the human helpers cite the same canonical procedures. over ~3 months this becomes the operating manual that makes the $1,500/mo magna role permanently unnecessary. directly protects the magna-transition savings ($18k/yr) by converting tribal knowledge into artifacts cheap humans and agents can execute. also shortens every future agent&#x27;s onboarding since sops become their system prompts."><summary><span class="t">Owner Decision-Capture Agent (recurring SOP scribe, beyond the one-time Magna brain-dump)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Cost avoidance: locks in the</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the already-proposed one-time Magna exit brain-dump: a recurring 15-minute weekly interview agent that asks the owner about decisions made that week (&#x27;why did you pick Flow over Higgsfield for that chapter?&#x27;, &#x27;what made that cover work?&#x27;), then writes or updates SOP documents in a /sops/ directory of the pipeline repo. Each SOP is tagged by role (GWHAR / Alternate / AI-agent) so other fleet agents and the human helpers cite the same canonical procedures. Over ~3 months this becomes the operating manual that makes the $1,500/mo Magna role permanently unnecessary.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Directly protects the Magna-transition savings ($18k/yr) by converting tribal knowledge into artifacts cheap humans and agents can execute. Also shortens every future agent&#x27;s onboarding since SOPs become their system prompts.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Cost avoidance: locks in the $1,500/mo assistant replacement permanently.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Magna transition context, ops ownership layer (ownerType routing), claude-comic-pipeline repo</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="fleet dispatcher agent (chief-of-staff + bridge.php agent-handoff protocol) the flagship meta-agent that turns individual agents into a department. phase 1 (weeks 1-2): extend bridge.php with agent-to-agent verbs — memo (structured findings), request-job (one agent commissions work from another), escalate (needs-owner flag) — alongside the existing claim/genspec/heartbeat/done. phase 2 (weeks 3-4): stand up an agent registry (role, cadence, token budget, last-run, output location) and pilot with 3 agents (pulse strategist, qa librarian, competitive-intel) exchanging memos. phase 3 (month 2): add per-agent token/credit budget enforcement and run telemetry, route all escalations into a single owner-facing lane in ops.php. phase 4: onboard the rest of the fleet, so e.g. competitive-intel&#x27;s pricing findings auto-flow to pricing architect without owner plumbing. this is the multiplier on every other idea in this list: without a dispatcher, n agents means n daily check-ins for the owner; with it, one escalation lane. caps runaway token spend and makes the fleet auditable — the difference between 3 agents and 12 being sustainable."><summary><span class="t">Fleet Dispatcher Agent (chief-of-staff + bridge.php agent-handoff protocol)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Enabler: makes the whole rev</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The flagship meta-agent that turns individual agents into a department. Phase 1 (weeks 1-2): extend bridge.php with agent-to-agent verbs — memo (structured findings), request-job (one agent commissions work from another), escalate (needs-owner flag) — alongside the existing claim/genspec/heartbeat/done. Phase 2 (weeks 3-4): stand up an agent registry (role, cadence, token budget, last-run, output location) and pilot with 3 agents (Pulse Strategist, QA Librarian, Competitive-Intel) exchanging memos. Phase 3 (month 2): add per-agent token/credit budget enforcement and run telemetry, route all escalations into a single owner-facing lane in ops.php. Phase 4: onboard the rest of the fleet, so e.g. Competitive-Intel&#x27;s pricing findings auto-flow to Pricing Architect without owner plumbing.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> This is the multiplier on every other idea in this list: without a dispatcher, N agents means N daily check-ins for the owner; with it, one escalation lane. Caps runaway token spend and makes the fleet auditable — the difference between 3 agents and 12 being sustainable.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Enabler: makes the whole revenue/churn agent fleet operable by a solo owner.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php claim/genspec/heartbeat/done protocol, ops.php ownerType layer, worker.py scaffold</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="monthly board-meeting agent (owner&#x27;s board pack) distinct from the daily morning digest already proposed: on the 1st of each month this agent compiles a strategic board pack from all fleet memos plus pulse and cost data — per-property mini p&amp;l (pledges minus higgsfield/seedance credits and helper pay), kpi deltas vs. last month, experiment readouts, and the top 5 decisions awaiting the owner, each framed as multiple-choice options per the standing poll-on-high-stakes preference. rendered as a single studio page (studio/board.php) with a 10-minute-read discipline, and every chosen option auto-files as ops.php tasks. gives a solo operator the monthly altitude a real publisher&#x27;s board would force. decision latency on pricing, cadence, and property investment drops from &#x27;whenever it surfaces&#x27; to a fixed monthly cycle — historically where solo creators leak the most revenue."><summary><span class="t">Monthly Board-Meeting Agent (owner&#x27;s board pack)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Indirect but structural: for</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Distinct from the daily morning digest already proposed: on the 1st of each month this agent compiles a strategic board pack from all fleet memos plus Pulse and cost data — per-property mini P&amp;L (pledges minus Higgsfield/Seedance credits and helper pay), KPI deltas vs. last month, experiment readouts, and the top 5 decisions awaiting the owner, each framed as multiple-choice options per the standing poll-on-high-stakes preference. Rendered as a single studio page (studio/board.php) with a 10-minute-read discipline, and every chosen option auto-files as ops.php tasks.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Gives a solo operator the monthly altitude a real publisher&#x27;s board would force. Decision latency on pricing, cadence, and property investment drops from &#x27;whenever it surfaces&#x27; to a fixed monthly cycle — historically where solo creators leak the most revenue.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Indirect but structural: forces monthly revenue-decision throughput.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Fleet memos via bridge.php, Creator Pulse, per-chapter cost ledger data, poll-on-high-stakes pattern</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="churn-autopsy agent (cancellation forensics, beyond early-warning dms) goes beyond the already-proposed churn early-warning/win-back dms (an intervention tool): this is the diagnostic layer. monthly it pulls every cancellation across the 4 accounts from pulse, joins tenure, tier, join-source (via attribution.php), and days-since-last-release at cancel time, then produces cohort survival curves and a ranked, evidence-backed &#x27;why they leave&#x27; hypothesis list (e.g. &#x27;patrons joining mid-hiatus churn 2x by day 45&#x27;). each top hypothesis is handed to the retention experiment runner as a testable brief via the bridge memo verb. you cannot fix churn you have not diagnosed. if autopsies reveal even one structural leak — e.g. a release-gap-sensitive cohort — fixing it plausibly cuts monthly churn 1-2 points, compounding to 10-20% higher patron ltv."><summary><span class="t">Churn-Autopsy Agent (cancellation forensics, beyond early-warning DMs)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention/LTV: converts chur</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the already-proposed churn early-warning/win-back DMs (an intervention tool): this is the diagnostic layer. Monthly it pulls every cancellation across the 4 accounts from Pulse, joins tenure, tier, join-source (via attribution.php), and days-since-last-release at cancel time, then produces cohort survival curves and a ranked, evidence-backed &#x27;why they leave&#x27; hypothesis list (e.g. &#x27;patrons joining mid-hiatus churn 2x by day 45&#x27;). Each top hypothesis is handed to the Retention Experiment Runner as a testable brief via the bridge memo verb.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> You cannot fix churn you have not diagnosed. If autopsies reveal even one structural leak — e.g. a release-gap-sensitive cohort — fixing it plausibly cuts monthly churn 1-2 points, compounding to 10-20% higher patron LTV.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention/LTV: converts churn from a number into ranked, testable causes.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse cancellation data, attribution.php join-source, bridge.php memo handoff</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="retention experiment runner agent (structured a/b program across 4 accounts) a flagship agent that runs retention as a science program using the 4 patreon accounts as natural test cells. phase 1 (weeks 1-2): build the metric harness on pulse — per-account weekly retention curves with enough history to detect effects. phase 2 (weeks 3-4): create an experiment registry and templates (release day-of-week, teaser cadence, chapter length, cliffhanger vs. resolution endings, growth-scene density per the locked growgetter spec). phase 3 (months 2-3): run one experiment per account per month — the agent writes the playbook, alternate/owner executes the posts, the agent measures 4-8 week retention deltas and publishes readouts. phase 4: winners get codified as sops via the decision-capture agent. cadence and structure choices are currently vibes; this makes them evidence. a single validated win — e.g. optimal release rhythm cutting churn 1.5 points on the flagship — is worth roughly 15%+ ltv on growgetter, the largest revenue line."><summary><span class="t">Retention Experiment Runner Agent (structured A/B program across 4 accounts)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Retention: systematic experi</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A flagship agent that runs retention as a science program using the 4 Patreon accounts as natural test cells. Phase 1 (weeks 1-2): build the metric harness on Pulse — per-account weekly retention curves with enough history to detect effects. Phase 2 (weeks 3-4): create an experiment registry and templates (release day-of-week, teaser cadence, chapter length, cliffhanger vs. resolution endings, growth-scene density per the locked GrowGetter spec). Phase 3 (months 2-3): run one experiment per account per month — the agent writes the playbook, Alternate/owner executes the posts, the agent measures 4-8 week retention deltas and publishes readouts. Phase 4: winners get codified as SOPs via the Decision-Capture agent.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Cadence and structure choices are currently vibes; this makes them evidence. A single validated win — e.g. optimal release rhythm cutting churn 1.5 points on the flagship — is worth roughly 15%+ LTV on GrowGetter, the largest revenue line.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Retention: systematic experimentation on the levers that drive patron lifetime.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse, Churn-Autopsy hypotheses via bridge.php, Alternate&#x27;s posting role, GrowGetter growth-density mandate</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="back-catalog merchandiser agent (off-patreon product line, beyond the vault tier) goes beyond the already-proposed vault tier (back-catalog inside patreon): this agent builds an off-patreon one-time-purchase product line, hedging platform risk. phase 1 (weeks 1-3): inventory the full catalog including the 8,840-gen higgsfield archive, cluster into themed bundles (per-character collections, &#x27;complete growth arcs&#x27;, best-of anthologies). phase 2 (weeks 4-6): for each bundle, assemble a print-ready pdf via the page-composer skill, draft a sales page, and stand up storefront listings (gumroad or itch.io — owner picks via multiple-choice) with attribution-tagged links from the site. phase 3 (month 2+): monthly it ships one new bundle, tracks per-bundle revenue, and prunes losers. all listings go live only with per-item owner approval per the no-post rule. new revenue stream from zero-marginal-cost inventory. comparable adult-comic creators do $200-800/mo on back-catalog pdfs; even the low end adds 10%+ to revenue while diversifying away from patreon dependence."><summary><span class="t">Back-Catalog Merchandiser Agent (off-Patreon product line, beyond the Vault tier)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream: one-time purchas</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the already-proposed Vault tier (back-catalog inside Patreon): this agent builds an off-Patreon one-time-purchase product line, hedging platform risk. Phase 1 (weeks 1-3): inventory the full catalog including the 8,840-gen Higgsfield archive, cluster into themed bundles (per-character collections, &#x27;complete growth arcs&#x27;, best-of anthologies). Phase 2 (weeks 4-6): for each bundle, assemble a print-ready PDF via the page-composer skill, draft a sales page, and stand up storefront listings (Gumroad or itch.io — owner picks via multiple-choice) with attribution-tagged links from the site. Phase 3 (month 2+): monthly it ships one new bundle, tracks per-bundle revenue, and prunes losers. All listings go live only with per-item owner approval per the no-post rule.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> New revenue stream from zero-marginal-cost inventory. Comparable adult-comic creators do $200-800/mo on back-catalog PDFs; even the low end adds 10%+ to revenue while diversifying away from Patreon dependence.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream: one-time purchases monetizing existing assets outside Patreon.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Higgsfield archive inventory via show_generations paging, page-composer skill, attribution.php, no-post approval rule</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="commission desk agent (runs the commission business, beyond the intake funnel) goes beyond the already-proposed intake funnel (a form): this agent operates the whole desk. it maintains a public price sheet, drafts quotes from inquiry details, converts accepted briefs into pipeline-ready genspecs (script-breakdown skill → bridge.php jobs), reserves production slots so commissions never collide with chapter deadlines, drafts client progress updates for approval, and keeps a margin ledger per commission using real credit costs. monthly it reports whether the price sheet needs raising based on demand and margin. commissions are currently &#x27;occasional&#x27; because every one costs owner attention; making them near-zero-overhead makes them steady. at 3-4 commissions/month at $100-200 with the proven overnight-run capacity, that is $300-800/mo of new revenue at healthy margin."><summary><span class="t">Commission Desk Agent (runs the commission business, beyond the intake funnel)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ New stream + ARPU: converts </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the already-proposed intake funnel (a form): this agent operates the whole desk. It maintains a public price sheet, drafts quotes from inquiry details, converts accepted briefs into pipeline-ready genspecs (script-breakdown skill → bridge.php jobs), reserves production slots so commissions never collide with chapter deadlines, drafts client progress updates for approval, and keeps a margin ledger per commission using real credit costs. Monthly it reports whether the price sheet needs raising based on demand and margin.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Commissions are currently &#x27;occasional&#x27; because every one costs owner attention; making them near-zero-overhead makes them steady. At 3-4 commissions/month at $100-200 with the proven overnight-run capacity, that is $300-800/mo of new revenue at healthy margin.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> New stream + ARPU: converts spare pipeline capacity into paid custom work.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> script-breakdown skill, bridge.php genspec jobs, proven 44-panel autonomous run, per-chapter cost ledger data</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="audience-growth agent (twitter/ig launch operator, beyond the syndicator) goes beyond the already-proposed mechanical syndicator/teaser tools (the hands): this agent is the strategist that finally executes the planned twitter/ig launch. phase 1 (weeks 1-2): account setup checklist for the owner, sfw crop guidelines derived from each property&#x27;s style, and a 30-day content calendar tied to the release pipeline. phase 2 (weeks 3-6): daily it drafts posts (crop + caption + utm-tagged link) into the approval queue — nothing posts without per-item ok — and weekly reads engagement + attribution.php conversions to adjust the calendar. phase 3 (month 2+): doubles down on the formats that convert to patrons, and hands proven formats to alternate as a routine posting packet. twitter is the dominant discovery channel in this niche and the operation has zero presence. comparable creators convert social followers to patrons at 0.5-2%; a year-one audience of 3-5k followers plausibly adds 30-75 patrons (~$150-400/mo)."><summary><span class="t">Audience-Growth Agent (Twitter/IG launch operator, beyond the syndicator)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Conversion: opens the larges</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Goes beyond the already-proposed mechanical syndicator/teaser tools (the hands): this agent is the strategist that finally executes the planned Twitter/IG launch. Phase 1 (weeks 1-2): account setup checklist for the owner, SFW crop guidelines derived from each property&#x27;s style, and a 30-day content calendar tied to the release pipeline. Phase 2 (weeks 3-6): daily it drafts posts (crop + caption + UTM-tagged link) into the approval queue — nothing posts without per-item OK — and weekly reads engagement + attribution.php conversions to adjust the calendar. Phase 3 (month 2+): doubles down on the formats that convert to patrons, and hands proven formats to Alternate as a routine posting packet.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Twitter is the dominant discovery channel in this niche and the operation has zero presence. Comparable creators convert social followers to patrons at 0.5-2%; a year-one audience of 3-5k followers plausibly adds 30-75 patrons (~$150-400/mo).</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Conversion: opens the largest untapped top-of-funnel in the niche.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> attribution.php UTM funnel, Alternate&#x27;s posting role, release pipeline as content source, no-post approval rule</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="superfan concierge agent (whale-tier crm) distinct from the already-proposed new-patron welcome sequence (onboarding): this agent manages the top decile. it scores patrons by tenure × tier × engagement (pulse + discord activity), maintains a superfan crm file, and drafts personal touches for approval — pledge-anniversary thank-yous, early wip peeks, a name-a-background-character offer. it also drafts the business case and perk design for a $25-50 &#x27;inner circle&#x27; tier (monthly input on story direction, printed-name credits page) targeted only at identified whales, presented to the owner as a multiple-choice launch proposal. in creator businesses the top 10% of fans routinely carry 30-40% of revenue. converting even 8-10 superfans to a $30 tier adds ~$200-250/mo, and personal-touch treatment makes the highest-value patrons the least likely to churn."><summary><span class="t">Superfan Concierge Agent (whale-tier CRM)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU + retention: whale iden</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Distinct from the already-proposed new-patron welcome sequence (onboarding): this agent manages the top decile. It scores patrons by tenure × tier × engagement (Pulse + Discord activity), maintains a superfan CRM file, and drafts personal touches for approval — pledge-anniversary thank-yous, early WIP peeks, a name-a-background-character offer. It also drafts the business case and perk design for a $25-50 &#x27;Inner Circle&#x27; tier (monthly input on story direction, printed-name credits page) targeted only at identified whales, presented to the owner as a multiple-choice launch proposal.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> In creator businesses the top 10% of fans routinely carry 30-40% of revenue. Converting even 8-10 superfans to a $30 tier adds ~$200-250/mo, and personal-touch treatment makes the highest-value patrons the least likely to churn.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU + retention: whale identification, whale tier, and whale-grade personal touch.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse patron data, Discord activity signals, poll-on-high-stakes pattern</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="fleet" data-eff="S" data-hor="days" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="credit quartermaster agent (spend forecasting + backend arbitrage) a daily agent that reads the higgsfield credit balance and transaction log via mcp, flow quota state, and per-chapter cost ledger data, then forecasts burn against the release calendar. it enforces the house cost rules mechanically (1k resolution, count=1, seedance mini-480p for iteration), flags anomalies like retry storms or a chapter tracking 2x budget mid-production, and recommends per-job routing between free flow and paid higgsfield based on each job&#x27;s nsfw-filter risk profile. weekly it posts a one-line spend-vs-forecast status; it only escalates when forecast breaches budget. generation credits are the largest variable cost and currently only visible after the fact. catching one retry storm or misrouted batch per month plausibly saves 10-20% of credit spend, directly widening per-chapter margin."><summary><span class="t">Credit Quartermaster Agent (spend forecasting + backend arbitrage)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Agent Fleet</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">days</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ Margin: real-time cost contr</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A daily agent that reads the Higgsfield credit balance and transaction log via MCP, Flow quota state, and per-chapter cost ledger data, then forecasts burn against the release calendar. It enforces the house cost rules mechanically (1k resolution, count=1, Seedance mini-480p for iteration), flags anomalies like retry storms or a chapter tracking 2x budget mid-production, and recommends per-job routing between free Flow and paid Higgsfield based on each job&#x27;s NSFW-filter risk profile. Weekly it posts a one-line spend-vs-forecast status; it only escalates when forecast breaches budget.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Generation credits are the largest variable cost and currently only visible after the fact. Catching one retry storm or misrouted batch per month plausibly saves 10-20% of credit spend, directly widening per-chapter margin.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> Margin: real-time cost control on the biggest variable expense.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Higgsfield MCP balance/transactions, per-chapter cost ledger data, house defaults (1k/count=1/mini-480p), Flow vs Higgsfield dual-backend setup</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="community"><h3>Community <span class="n">16</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="growverse: unified discord with 4-account tier-sync and locked-channel upsell build one unified discord server with per-property categories (growgetter, maxx, bloom, poweredheroes, mgai) and connect all four patreon accounts&#x27; discord integrations to it, so a patron of any account auto-gets the matching role — with visible stacked roles (&#x27;double grower&#x27;, &#x27;triple grower&#x27;) for multi-account patrons. phase 1: design channel/role architecture and wire the four patreon-discord integrations. phase 2: migrate existing members with a launch event. phase 3: non-patrons can see locked patron channels (names + pinned teaser, unreadable content) so every property lounge is a standing cross-sell surface. phase 4: automod + alternate as day-to-day steward, with creator pulse role-audit so revoked patrons lose roles. discord-linked patrons see daily value between monthly chapter drops and churn measurably less; locked-channel visibility plus stacked-role status is a permanent cross-patreon upsell. at ~500 patrons, if 30% link and cross-account conversion adds 3-5% multi-account patrons, that is roughly $100-250/mo new plus a durable churn reduction."><summary><span class="t">Growverse: unified Discord with 4-account tier-sync and locked-channel upsell</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ conversion (cross-account up</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Build one unified Discord server with per-property categories (GrowGetter, Maxx, Bloom, PoweredHeroes, MGAI) and connect ALL FOUR Patreon accounts&#x27; Discord integrations to it, so a patron of any account auto-gets the matching role — with visible stacked roles (&#x27;Double Grower&#x27;, &#x27;Triple Grower&#x27;) for multi-account patrons. Phase 1: design channel/role architecture and wire the four Patreon-Discord integrations. Phase 2: migrate existing members with a launch event. Phase 3: non-patrons can SEE locked patron channels (names + pinned teaser, unreadable content) so every property lounge is a standing cross-sell surface. Phase 4: automod + Alternate as day-to-day steward, with Creator Pulse role-audit so revoked patrons lose roles.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Discord-linked patrons see daily value between monthly chapter drops and churn measurably less; locked-channel visibility plus stacked-role status is a permanent cross-Patreon upsell. At ~500 patrons, if 30% link and cross-account conversion adds 3-5% multi-account patrons, that is roughly $100-250/mo new plus a durable churn reduction.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> conversion (cross-account upsell) + retention (daily touchpoint)</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse 4-account rollup (role auditing); goes beyond the excluded &#x27;unified Discord notifier&#x27; — that posts messages, this is the server architecture and tier-sync layer the notifier posts into</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="XL" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="fork the growth: patron-voted branching canon with monetized what-if branches at key cliffhangers, patrons vote which growth path the story takes — and both branches get produced, because the autonomous overnight pipeline makes the losing branch nearly free. the winner continues canon; the loser ships as a &#x27;what if&#x27; exclusive on a higher tier, so contested votes directly mint premium content. phase 1: manual pilot on one growgetter cliffhanger with a simple patreon+discord vote. phase 2: studio/branch.php to define fork points and tally weighted votes (inner circle x3 weight). phase 3: auto-genspec both branches through bridge.php overnight runs. phase 4: package losing branches as the &#x27;what if vault&#x27; perk on a $15+ tier. voting on a story that actually forks is the strongest engagement mechanic in serial fiction, and the what-if exclusive gives a concrete tier-upgrade reason. if 10% of ~500 patrons upgrade +$5 for what-ifs, that is ~$250/mo, plus vote windows create recurring can&#x27;t-miss moments that suppress churn."><summary><span class="t">Fork the Growth: patron-voted branching canon with monetized What-If branches</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort XL</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU via What-If tier upgrad</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>At key cliffhangers, patrons vote which growth path the story takes — and BOTH branches get produced, because the autonomous overnight pipeline makes the losing branch nearly free. The winner continues canon; the loser ships as a &#x27;What If&#x27; exclusive on a higher tier, so contested votes directly mint premium content. Phase 1: manual pilot on one GrowGetter cliffhanger with a simple Patreon+Discord vote. Phase 2: studio/branch.php to define fork points and tally weighted votes (Inner Circle x3 weight). Phase 3: auto-genspec both branches through bridge.php overnight runs. Phase 4: package losing branches as the &#x27;What If Vault&#x27; perk on a $15+ tier.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Voting on a story that actually forks is the strongest engagement mechanic in serial fiction, and the What-If exclusive gives a concrete tier-upgrade reason. If 10% of ~500 patrons upgrade +$5 for What-Ifs, that is ~$250/mo, plus vote windows create recurring can&#x27;t-miss moments that suppress churn.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU via What-If tier upgrades + retention via vote events</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php worker protocol, proven 44-panel overnight runs, script-breakdown skill; explicitly goes beyond the excluded &#x27;monthly patron story polls&#x27; — polls advise, this forks canon and productizes the losing branch</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="milestone muscle: patron-count milestones literally trigger a character&#x27;s growth stages a communal character whose growth stages unlock at patron-count milestones (&#x27;at 450 patrons she reaches stage 5&#x27;), with a live tracker on 3dmusclecomics.com and a discord progress bot. joining patreon becomes the mechanism of the transformation — the audience collectively grows her. phase 1: design the character and a 10-stage ladder using the over-spec size-guide conventions. phase 2: public tracker page fed by creator pulse&#x27;s daily sync + discord progress announcements. phase 3: auto-render and auto-post each unlocked stage within 24h of the milestone via bridge.php. phase 4: seasonal ladder resets and per-property variants (a bloom ladder, a poweredheroes ladder). converts the growth fantasy itself into a conversion engine; &#x27;only 12 patrons until stage 6&#x27; is urgent and shareable. plausibly worth a 5-10% patron-count lift while a ladder is hot — 25-50 patrons x ~$8 avg = $200-400/mo — and it gives fans a reason to recruit."><summary><span class="t">Milestone Muscle: patron-count milestones literally trigger a character&#x27;s growth stages</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ new-patron conversion via co</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A communal character whose growth stages unlock at patron-count milestones (&#x27;at 450 patrons she reaches Stage 5&#x27;), with a live tracker on 3dmusclecomics.com and a Discord progress bot. Joining Patreon becomes the mechanism of the transformation — the audience collectively grows her. Phase 1: design the character and a 10-stage ladder using the over-spec size-guide conventions. Phase 2: public tracker page fed by Creator Pulse&#x27;s daily sync + Discord progress announcements. Phase 3: auto-render and auto-post each unlocked stage within 24h of the milestone via bridge.php. Phase 4: seasonal ladder resets and per-property variants (a Bloom ladder, a PoweredHeroes ladder).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts the growth fantasy itself into a conversion engine; &#x27;only 12 patrons until Stage 6&#x27; is urgent and shareable. Plausibly worth a 5-10% patron-count lift while a ladder is hot — 25-50 patrons x ~$8 avg = $200-400/mo — and it gives fans a reason to recruit.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> new-patron conversion via collective milestone mechanic</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse daily sync (patron counts), bridge.php genspec workers, growth-density mandate; distinct from excluded &#x27;public teaser pages&#x27; — this is a live communal game, not a teaser funnel</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="cameo engine: &#x27;get written into the comic&#x27; capped top tier a $40-50/mo tier capped at 10-15 seats where the patron&#x27;s oc (or stylized self) appears as a named background character in upcoming chapters, plus they receive their character&#x27;s full sheet render. phase 1: manual pilot with 2-3 known superfans — form intake, character sheets hand-run with the pipeline&#x27;s character-lock lessons. phase 2: studio/cameo.php intake queue with per-chapter slot scheduling and a qa gate so cameos pass the no-extras rule as deliberate, counted cast. phase 3: tier launch on growgetter + maxx. phase 4: upsell ladder — cameo → speaking role → starring one-shot mini as a premium commission. 10 seats x $45 = ~$450/mo at near-pure margin (credits + one qa pass), and cameo patrons are maximally retained — cancelling kills their character. also generates organic word-of-mouth (&#x27;that&#x27;s my character in panel 3&#x27;)."><summary><span class="t">Cameo Engine: &#x27;Get Written Into the Comic&#x27; capped top tier</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ new high-ARPU capped tier + </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A $40-50/mo tier capped at 10-15 seats where the patron&#x27;s OC (or stylized self) appears as a named background character in upcoming chapters, plus they receive their character&#x27;s full sheet render. Phase 1: manual pilot with 2-3 known superfans — form intake, character sheets hand-run with the pipeline&#x27;s character-lock lessons. Phase 2: studio/cameo.php intake queue with per-chapter slot scheduling and a QA gate so cameos pass the no-extras rule as deliberate, counted cast. Phase 3: tier launch on GrowGetter + Maxx. Phase 4: upsell ladder — cameo → speaking role → starring one-shot mini as a premium commission.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> 10 seats x $45 = ~$450/mo at near-pure margin (credits + one QA pass), and cameo patrons are maximally retained — cancelling kills their character. Also generates organic word-of-mouth (&#x27;that&#x27;s MY character in panel 3&#x27;).</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> new high-ARPU capped tier + retention lock-in</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> creator.php cockpit, character-lock + no-background-extras lessons, ck_ai_qa defect scan; distinct from excluded Fan Art Friday — that reposts fan art, this renders fans INTO canon</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="pipeline cam: auto-captured &#x27;making of&#x27; timelapse per chapter — mid-tier perk + youtube funnel the pipeline is genuinely spectacular (overnight 44-panel runs, ai qa defect flags, keep/trash calls) and fans love seeing how it&#x27;s made. phase 1: have bridge.php workers retain per-chapter intermediates (genspecs, rejected variants, qa flags) — they already exist, just archive them. phase 2: an ffmpeg compositor auto-assembles a 3-5 minute prompt→variants→winner→lettered-page timelapse per chapter, reusing the contact-sheet tooling. phase 3: monthly &#x27;director&#x27;s cut&#x27; bts drop for the $10+ tier. phase 4: sfw cuts to a new youtube channel as top-of-funnel, with attribution.php utms on every description link. a zero-marginal-cost perk that hardens the mid tier, plus an evergreen acquisition surface — &#x27;how ai comics actually get made&#x27; is a proven youtube niche. even a modest channel adding 5-15 patrons/mo is $40-120/mo compounding, and the perk supports a mid-tier price raise."><summary><span class="t">Pipeline Cam: auto-captured &#x27;making of&#x27; timelapse per chapter — mid-tier perk + YouTube funnel</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU (mid-tier perk) + new a</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The pipeline is genuinely spectacular (overnight 44-panel runs, AI QA defect flags, keep/trash calls) and fans love seeing how it&#x27;s made. Phase 1: have bridge.php workers retain per-chapter intermediates (genspecs, rejected variants, QA flags) — they already exist, just archive them. Phase 2: an ffmpeg compositor auto-assembles a 3-5 minute prompt→variants→winner→lettered-page timelapse per chapter, reusing the contact-sheet tooling. Phase 3: monthly &#x27;Director&#x27;s Cut&#x27; BTS drop for the $10+ tier. Phase 4: SFW cuts to a new YouTube channel as top-of-funnel, with attribution.php UTMs on every description link.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> A zero-marginal-cost perk that hardens the mid tier, plus an evergreen acquisition surface — &#x27;how AI comics actually get made&#x27; is a proven YouTube niche. Even a modest channel adding 5-15 patrons/mo is $40-120/mo compounding, and the perk supports a mid-tier price raise.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU (mid-tier perk) + new acquisition channel (YouTube)</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php, Seedance/ffmpeg contact-sheet tooling, attribution.php; distinct from excluded &#x27;auto-trailer per release&#x27; — trailers promote the product, this packages the process</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="L" data-hor="month+" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="growfest: semi-annual one-week community festival a programmed event week run twice a year: daily page drops (front-loaded via overnight runs), the caption-contest final, the character foundry winner reveal, a director&#x27;s-commentary ama, the fork-the-growth vote finale, and a 7-day launch discount on annual memberships. phase 1: lock the program and pre-produce all assets in the two weeks prior. phase 2: build the posting calendar as an alternate-executable packet (every post pre-drafted, owner approves outbound per policy). phase 3: run the week with a live discord energy loop (progress bars, hourly winners). phase 4: retro via attribution.php + creator pulse to measure conversion and decide cadence. event weeks concentrate attention and give lapsed fans a re-entry moment; a well-run festival plausibly adds 20-40 patrons ($160-320/mo) and reactivates a similar number of churned ones, while producing a reusable playbook."><summary><span class="t">GrowFest: semi-annual one-week community festival</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-hor c-month">month+</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ conversion spike + reactivat</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A programmed event week run twice a year: daily page drops (front-loaded via overnight runs), the caption-contest final, the Character Foundry winner reveal, a director&#x27;s-commentary AMA, the Fork-the-Growth vote finale, and a 7-day launch discount on annual memberships. Phase 1: lock the program and pre-produce all assets in the two weeks prior. Phase 2: build the posting calendar as an Alternate-executable packet (every post pre-drafted, owner approves outbound per policy). Phase 3: run the week with a live Discord energy loop (progress bars, hourly winners). Phase 4: retro via attribution.php + Creator Pulse to measure conversion and decide cadence.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Event weeks concentrate attention and give lapsed fans a re-entry moment; a well-run festival plausibly adds 20-40 patrons ($160-320/mo) and reactivates a similar number of churned ones, while producing a reusable playbook.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> conversion spike + reactivation of lapsed patrons</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> attribution.php for measurement, Creator Pulse for before/after, ops.php for the task packet; composes the contest/vote/AMA ideas in this wave into one revenue spike</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="chapter credits hall of fame with tenure badges page-composer appends an auto-generated credits page to every chapter: opt-in patron names grouped by tier, with tenure badges (&#x27;founding grower&#x27; 24mo+, &#x27;veteran&#x27; 12mo+), pulled from creator pulse. a matching /hall-of-fame page on 3dmusclecomics.com regenerates on each deploy. superfans see their name permanently printed in the work they funded. public tenure recognition creates loss aversion at cancel time — churning means falling out of the credits. bonus: credits pages travel with pirated copies, turning piracy into an ad for patronage. plausible 1-2 point churn reduction on the recognized cohort."><summary><span class="t">Chapter Credits Hall of Fame with tenure badges</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ retention via public status</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Page-composer appends an auto-generated credits page to every chapter: opt-in patron names grouped by tier, with tenure badges (&#x27;Founding Grower&#x27; 24mo+, &#x27;Veteran&#x27; 12mo+), pulled from Creator Pulse. A matching /hall-of-fame page on 3dmusclecomics.com regenerates on each deploy. Superfans see their name permanently printed in the work they funded.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Public tenure recognition creates loss aversion at cancel time — churning means falling out of the credits. Bonus: credits pages travel with pirated copies, turning piracy into an ad for patronage. Plausible 1-2 point churn reduction on the recognized cohort.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> retention via public status</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> page-composer skill, Creator Pulse tenure data, comics.js manifest deploy flow</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="S" data-hor="days" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="cutting room floor: monthly near-miss gallery perk from the trash folders every chapter already produces dozens of near-miss variants preserved by the trash-to-subfolder policy plus qa-flagged before/after pairs. a packager script bundles the best 10-15 per month into a &#x27;cutting room floor&#x27; gallery post for the $10 tier — annotated with one line on why each was cut. zero new generation cost; the content already exists on disk. strengthens the mid-tier value story enough to support a $2-3 price raise or upgrade nudge; at 50 mid-tier patrons taking +$2, that is ~$100/mo for a few hours of scripting."><summary><span class="t">Cutting Room Floor: monthly near-miss gallery perk from the trash folders</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">days</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ ARPU via mid-tier value stac</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Every chapter already produces dozens of near-miss variants preserved by the trash-to-subfolder policy plus QA-flagged before/after pairs. A packager script bundles the best 10-15 per month into a &#x27;Cutting Room Floor&#x27; gallery post for the $10 tier — annotated with one line on why each was cut. Zero new generation cost; the content already exists on disk.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Strengthens the mid-tier value story enough to support a $2-3 price raise or upgrade nudge; at 50 mid-tier patrons taking +$2, that is ~$100/mo for a few hours of scripting.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> ARPU via mid-tier value stacking</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> trash/ subfolder convention, ck_ai_qa flags, review-composite tooling; distinct from the excluded Vault tier — that is published back-catalog, this is never-published material</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="S" data-hor="days" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="weekly caption contest with winner lettered into canon panel each week, pull one dramatic textless panel from the 8,840-generation higgsfield archive, post it to discord + deviantart, fans submit captions, patrons vote, and the winning caption gets professionally lettered into the panel via page-composer and posted with the winner credited. alternate handles posting (owner approves outbound), ai handles panel selection and lettering. a near-zero-cost weekly ritual that keeps the community&#x27;s clock ticking between chapter drops, and every captioned winner is natively shareable acquisition content. cheap, compounding engagement."><summary><span class="t">Weekly caption contest with winner lettered into canon panel</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">days</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ retention ritual + shareable</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Each week, pull one dramatic textless panel from the 8,840-generation Higgsfield archive, post it to Discord + DeviantArt, fans submit captions, patrons vote, and the winning caption gets professionally lettered into the panel via page-composer and posted with the winner credited. Alternate handles posting (owner approves outbound), AI handles panel selection and lettering.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> A near-zero-cost weekly ritual that keeps the community&#x27;s clock ticking between chapter drops, and every captioned winner is natively shareable acquisition content. Cheap, compounding engagement.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> retention ritual + shareable top-of-funnel content</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Higgsfield show_generations archive paging, page-composer lettering, bake-dialogue conventions</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="S" data-hor="days" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="inner circle: $50/mo superfan council capped at 10 a hard-capped identity tier: private discord channel, monthly premise-input session with the owner, name-a-character rights, x3 weight in fork-the-growth votes, and a permanent inner circle line in every chapter&#x27;s credits. scarcity (10 seats, waitlist) does the selling. launch is mostly configuration: tier setup on the growgetter patreon, role in the growverse server, credits hook. $500/mo at cap from the people most willing to pay, and council members essentially never churn — influence and identity are the strongest glue there is. waitlist visibility also anchors the value of lower tiers."><summary><span class="t">Inner Circle: $50/mo superfan council capped at 10</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">days</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:owner</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ new high-ARPU capped tier</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A hard-capped identity tier: private Discord channel, monthly premise-input session with the owner, name-a-character rights, x3 weight in Fork-the-Growth votes, and a permanent Inner Circle line in every chapter&#x27;s credits. Scarcity (10 seats, waitlist) does the selling. Launch is mostly configuration: tier setup on the GrowGetter Patreon, role in the Growverse server, credits hook.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> $500/mo at cap from the people most willing to pay, and council members essentially never churn — influence and identity are the strongest glue there is. Waitlist visibility also anchors the value of lower tiers.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> new high-ARPU capped tier</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Growverse roles, Hall of Fame credits hook, Fork-the-Growth vote weighting</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="character foundry: quarterly design contest where the winner joins the cast fans submit character design briefs (text form — heritage, build, growth flavor, wardrobe). gwhar shortlists 8-10 (exactly the character work he loves), the pipeline renders finalist sheets in the house photoreal style with proper character locks, patrons vote, and the winner becomes a recurring cast member with a &#x27;created by&#x27; credit in every appearance. entry open to all; voting patron-only. a quarterly engagement spike with patron-gated voting as a conversion nudge, plus a steady community-sourced oc feed into the ideator gap of the 7-stage production vision. the winner&#x27;s creator becomes a permanent evangelist."><summary><span class="t">Character Foundry: quarterly design contest where the winner joins the cast</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:GWHAR</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ conversion via patron-gated </span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Fans submit character design briefs (text form — heritage, build, growth flavor, wardrobe). GWHAR shortlists 8-10 (exactly the character work he loves), the pipeline renders finalist sheets in the house photoreal style with proper character locks, patrons vote, and the winner becomes a recurring cast member with a &#x27;created by&#x27; credit in every appearance. Entry open to all; voting patron-only.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> A quarterly engagement spike with patron-gated voting as a conversion nudge, plus a steady community-sourced OC feed into the ideator gap of the 7-stage production vision. The winner&#x27;s creator becomes a permanent evangelist.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> conversion via patron-gated voting + engagement</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> character-locks-must-be-vivid conventions, cast-lineup style propagation, production-system ideator gap; distinct from excluded Fan Art Friday (briefs rendered into canon cast, not art reposts) and beyond GWHAR story-scout intake (characters + render + vote + canon loop)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="community writers room with paid fast-track minis monthly premise thread in discord/patreon; gwhar shortlists 3; patrons vote; the winning premise is produced as an 8-page mini with &#x27;story by [fan]&#x27; credit — the proven overnight pipeline makes an 8-pager cheap. add a paid fast-track rung: $200 guarantees your premise gets produced as a mini regardless of the vote, a productized step below full commissions that plugs into the commission funnel rather than replacing it. the free track drives monthly participation; the fast-track creates a new $200-600/mo revenue rung if 1-3 sell monthly, at maybe 2-3 hours of human time each given pipeline automation."><summary><span class="t">Community Writers Room with paid fast-track minis</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ new stream: productized $200</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Monthly premise thread in Discord/Patreon; GWHAR shortlists 3; patrons vote; the winning premise is produced as an 8-page mini with &#x27;story by [fan]&#x27; credit — the proven overnight pipeline makes an 8-pager cheap. Add a paid fast-track rung: $200 guarantees your premise gets produced as a mini regardless of the vote, a productized step below full commissions that plugs into the commission funnel rather than replacing it.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The free track drives monthly participation; the fast-track creates a new $200-600/mo revenue rung if 1-3 sell monthly, at maybe 2-3 hours of human time each given pipeline automation.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> new stream: productized $200 fast-track minis</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> script-breakdown + comic-production skills, proven 44-panel overnight run, GWHAR&#x27;s story-reading strengths; beyond excluded commission-intake-funnel (that is bespoke intake, this is a community contest + fixed-price product)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="anniversary gift engine: personalized panel at renewal cliffs creator pulse already knows tenure. at each patron&#x27;s 6/12/24-month anniversary, auto-generate a personalized single celebratory panel — their favorite character (captured by a one-question onboarding survey) in a triumphant growth beat with their name lettered in — queued as a draft dm the owner approves and sends before the renewal date, per the no-outbound-without-approval rule. anniversaries are churn cliffs; a personalized gift landing days before renewal is a strong stay signal. at ~500 patrons, roughly 30-50 hit an anniversary monthly; saving even 2-3 would-be churners is $16-24/mo in protected mrr, compounding into meaningful ltv."><summary><span class="t">Anniversary Gift Engine: personalized panel at renewal cliffs</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ retention at the highest-ris</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Creator Pulse already knows tenure. At each patron&#x27;s 6/12/24-month anniversary, auto-generate a personalized single celebratory panel — their favorite character (captured by a one-question onboarding survey) in a triumphant growth beat with their name lettered in — queued as a draft DM the owner approves and sends before the renewal date, per the no-outbound-without-approval rule.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Anniversaries are churn cliffs; a personalized gift landing days before renewal is a strong stay signal. At ~500 patrons, roughly 30-50 hit an anniversary monthly; saving even 2-3 would-be churners is $16-24/mo in protected MRR, compounding into meaningful LTV.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> retention at the highest-risk renewal moments</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse tenure data, creator.php generation, bake-dialogue lettering; distinct from excluded churn early-warning win-backs (proactive gifting, not churn response)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="superfan index in creator pulse a new creator pulse section computing a per-patron superfan score: tenure x tier x patreon comment frequency x discord activity (via linked growverse roles). surfaces the actual top 20% for inner circle invites, cameo engine offers, contest judging, and testimonial asks — and flags &#x27;fading superfans&#x27; whose score is dropping for personal owner attention before they lapse. infrastructure that makes every other superfan play targeted instead of broadcast. knowing who the 20% are typically doubles the take-rate of high-ticket offers like cameo seats, and fading-superfan flags catch the most expensive churn (long-tenure, high-tier) early."><summary><span class="t">Superfan Index in Creator Pulse</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ conversion lift on high-ARPU</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A new Creator Pulse section computing a per-patron superfan score: tenure x tier x Patreon comment frequency x Discord activity (via linked Growverse roles). Surfaces the actual top 20% for Inner Circle invites, Cameo Engine offers, contest judging, and testimonial asks — and flags &#x27;fading superfans&#x27; whose score is dropping for personal owner attention before they lapse.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Infrastructure that makes every other superfan play targeted instead of broadcast. Knowing WHO the 20% are typically doubles the take-rate of high-ticket offers like cameo seats, and fading-superfan flags catch the most expensive churn (long-tenure, high-tier) early.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> conversion lift on high-ARPU offers + high-value churn prevention</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse 4-account sync on the Mac mini, Growverse role data</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="S" data-hor="days" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="early pages drip: serialize each chapter daily in a patron-only channel instead of dropping a finished chapter all at once, release 2-3 pages per day in a patron-only growverse channel ahead of the full patreon post, delivered through the existing webhook autopost mechanism. the chapter is already done — this is purely a release-cadence change that turns a monthly touchpoint into a daily habit loop with cliffhangers between drips. directly attacks read-then-churn behavior: there is always a chapter mid-drip, so there is never a clean moment to cancel. daily active presence in discord also feeds every contest and vote mechanic. plausible 1-3 point monthly churn reduction on drip readers."><summary><span class="t">Early Pages drip: serialize each chapter daily in a patron-only channel</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-hor">days</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ retention via habit loop and</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Instead of dropping a finished chapter all at once, release 2-3 pages per day in a patron-only Growverse channel ahead of the full Patreon post, delivered through the existing webhook autopost mechanism. The chapter is already done — this is purely a release-cadence change that turns a monthly touchpoint into a daily habit loop with cliffhangers between drips.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Directly attacks read-then-churn behavior: there is always a chapter mid-drip, so there is never a clean moment to cancel. Daily active presence in Discord also feeds every contest and vote mechanic. Plausible 1-3 point monthly churn reduction on drip readers.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> retention via habit loop and always-mid-story state</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Growverse channel architecture (idea 1), existing Discord webhook autopost as the delivery rail — this is the cadence/perk design layered on it</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="community" data-eff="M" data-hor="weeks" data-wave="2" data-rev="1" data-hay="panel of the month awards → year-end best-of anthology monthly patron vote on the best page across all properties (a 10-minute alternate posting task with pre-built composite ballots from the review-composite tooling). at year end, page-composer compiles the 12 winners plus vote stats and fan comments into a &#x27;best of 3dmc&#x27; pdf anthology sold as a one-time purchase ($10-15 via patreon one-off or gumroad). the monthly vote is a light ritual that doubles as quality telemetry on what fans actually love; the anthology is a genuinely new revenue stream — 100 buyers x $12 = ~$1,200 at year end, then an evergreen catalog item for every future new fan."><summary><span class="t">Panel of the Month awards → year-end Best-Of anthology</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Community</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-hor">weeks</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span><span class="chip c-rev">$ new stream: one-time antholo</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Monthly patron vote on the best page across all properties (a 10-minute Alternate posting task with pre-built composite ballots from the review-composite tooling). At year end, page-composer compiles the 12 winners plus vote stats and fan comments into a &#x27;Best of 3DMC&#x27; PDF anthology sold as a one-time purchase ($10-15 via Patreon one-off or Gumroad).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The monthly vote is a light ritual that doubles as quality telemetry on what fans actually love; the anthology is a genuinely new revenue stream — 100 buyers x $12 = ~$1,200 at year end, then an evergreen catalog item for every future new fan.</p><p class="revnote"><strong>Revenue mechanism:</strong> new stream: one-time anthology sales + engagement telemetry</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> review-composite tooling for ballots, page-composer PDF export, comics.js catalog for evergreen listing</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="automation"><h3>Automation <span class="n">10</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="night shift v1: promote worker.py to a launchd-managed always-on runner on the mac mini finish the worker.py scaffold in claude-comic-pipeline/studio/worker/ into a real daemon: install the existing com.3dmc.comicworker.plist with keepalive so launchd auto-restarts it, have it poll bridge.php claim/genspec/heartbeat/done in a loop, execute jobs via headless claude code sessions, and log every job to a local jobs.log plus a bridge-side run ledger. the mac mini already proves the pattern with the creator pulse daily sync; this makes it a 24/7 job-drainer instead of a once-a-day script. this is the keystone every other loop plugs into: the proven 44-panel autonomous overnight run becomes the default mode of production, not a one-off. anything queued by 11pm is done by morning with zero supervision."><summary><span class="t">Night Shift v1: promote worker.py to a launchd-managed always-on runner on the Mac mini</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Finish the worker.py scaffold in claude-comic-pipeline/studio/worker/ into a real daemon: install the existing com.3dmc.comicworker.plist with KeepAlive so launchd auto-restarts it, have it poll bridge.php claim/genspec/heartbeat/done in a loop, execute jobs via headless Claude Code sessions, and log every job to a local jobs.log plus a bridge-side run ledger. The Mac mini already proves the pattern with the Creator Pulse daily sync; this makes it a 24/7 job-drainer instead of a once-a-day script.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> This is the keystone every other loop plugs into: the proven 44-panel autonomous overnight run becomes the default mode of production, not a one-off. Anything queued by 11pm is done by morning with zero supervision.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php worker protocol + worker.py scaffold + com.3dmc.comicworker.plist + Mac mini (Creator Pulse host)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="evening queue seeder: a planner job that decides what the runner does tonight a nightly 9pm cron (headless claude session) that reads the publish calendar and open work: unfinished chapters in the pipeline repo, pending import.php transform batches, ops.php tasks tagged ownertype=ai with an aiplan, and translation/redactor backlogs — then enqueues a prioritized set of bridge.php jobs sized to what the mini can finish overnight. writes a one-line plan note to cc.php so the morning digest can compare plan vs. actual. removes the owner as the nightly bottleneck: today nothing runs unless he manually queues it. with a seeder, the mini never idles and the 388-task backlog drains itself on autopilot."><summary><span class="t">Evening Queue Seeder: a planner job that decides what the runner does tonight</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A nightly 9pm cron (headless Claude session) that reads the publish calendar and open work: unfinished chapters in the pipeline repo, pending import.php transform batches, ops.php tasks tagged ownerType=AI with an aiPlan, and translation/redactor backlogs — then enqueues a prioritized set of bridge.php jobs sized to what the mini can finish overnight. Writes a one-line plan note to cc.php so the morning digest can compare plan vs. actual.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Removes the owner as the nightly bottleneck: today nothing runs unless he manually queues it. With a seeder, the mini never idles and the 388-task backlog drains itself on autopilot.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php + cc.php/ops.php (aiTag/aiPlan/ownerType fields) + import.php batches</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="watchdog + self-healing: stale-job requeue and a runner health banner in studio add a watchdog to bridge.php: jobs whose heartbeat is silent for n minutes get auto-requeued (with a retry cap and a dead-letter state); the runner records a &#x27;last seen&#x27; timestamp that cc.php surfaces as a green/red health banner. on the mini, launchd keepalive restarts crashes, and a tiny cron pings bridge.php — two missed check-ins triggers a push notification to the owner&#x27;s phone. makes unattended operation trustworthy: a wedged flow tab or crashed worker at 2am currently silently kills the whole night. with requeue + dead-letter + alerting, one bad job costs one retry, not eight hours."><summary><span class="t">Watchdog + self-healing: stale-job requeue and a runner health banner in Studio</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a watchdog to bridge.php: jobs whose heartbeat is silent for N minutes get auto-requeued (with a retry cap and a dead-letter state); the runner records a &#x27;last seen&#x27; timestamp that cc.php surfaces as a green/red health banner. On the mini, launchd KeepAlive restarts crashes, and a tiny cron pings bridge.php — two missed check-ins triggers a push notification to the owner&#x27;s phone.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Makes unattended operation trustworthy: a wedged Flow tab or crashed worker at 2am currently silently kills the whole night. With requeue + dead-letter + alerting, one bad job costs one retry, not eight hours.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php heartbeat verb + cc.php + launchd on the Mac mini</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="morning digest: one 7am report of everything that ran overnight a daily cron on the mini that compiles the bridge.php run ledger (jobs done/failed/requeued), ck_ai_qa defect counts on new panels, creator pulse deltas (new patrons, churn), spam cleared, and any watchdog alerts into a single discord dm or email with links into studio. include a thumbnail contact-sheet of overnight panels so the owner can approve-or-flag from his phone over coffee. turns &#x27;check six dashboards&#x27; into a 2-minute morning read; also the trust layer that lets the owner stop babysitting the runner. the notify-of-results half of the always-on vision."><summary><span class="t">Morning Digest: one 7am report of everything that ran overnight</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A daily cron on the mini that compiles the bridge.php run ledger (jobs done/failed/requeued), ck_ai_qa defect counts on new panels, Creator Pulse deltas (new patrons, churn), spam cleared, and any watchdog alerts into a single Discord DM or email with links into Studio. Include a thumbnail contact-sheet of overnight panels so the owner can approve-or-flag from his phone over coffee.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns &#x27;check six dashboards&#x27; into a 2-minute morning read; also the trust layer that lets the owner stop babysitting the runner. The notify-of-results half of the always-on vision.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php run ledger + creator.php ck_ai_qa + Creator Pulse</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="standing overnight transform conveyor with an auto-qa gate generalize the 44-panel autonomous win into a permanent lane: import.php snip output automatically enqueues &#x27;transform&#x27; jobs on bridge.php; the runner drains them nightly; each finished panel is auto-scanned by the ck_ai_qa defect check (priority: duplicate characters/extras) and failures are auto-requeued with the defect note injected into the retry genspec, up to 2 retries before landing in a human-review folder. ship it by wiring three existing pieces together, no new ui. the 2d-to-3d back-catalog conversion (a core magna duty) becomes a fire-and-forget conveyor: feed pdfs in the evening, review a mostly-clean batch in the morning. retry-with-defect-note should cut manual re-render passes by half or more."><summary><span class="t">Standing overnight transform conveyor with an auto-QA gate</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Generalize the 44-panel autonomous win into a permanent lane: import.php snip output automatically enqueues &#x27;transform&#x27; jobs on bridge.php; the runner drains them nightly; each finished panel is auto-scanned by the ck_ai_qa defect check (priority: duplicate characters/extras) and failures are auto-requeued with the defect note injected into the retry genspec, up to 2 retries before landing in a human-review folder. Ship it by wiring three existing pieces together, no new UI.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The 2D-to-3D back-catalog conversion (a core Magna duty) becomes a fire-and-forget conveyor: feed PDFs in the evening, review a mostly-clean batch in the morning. Retry-with-defect-note should cut manual re-render passes by half or more.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> import.php + bridge.php &#x27;transform&#x27; job kind + creator.php ck_ai_qa defect scan</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="translation conveyor: a &#x27;translate&#x27; job kind for the growgetter es/de/zh sop add a &#x27;translate&#x27; job kind to bridge.php that runs the already-defined sop unattended: strip a chapter script to dialogue-only, ai-translate to es/de/zh, and emit proofreader-ready packets (per-language docx + panel-reference sheet) into a handoff folder, plus a drafted upwork message per packet (draft only, never sent). seeder enqueues one chapter per night until the backlog clears. one of the 15 magna duties goes fully automatic except the final human proofread handoff; three languages of growgetter back-catalog become a queue that drains itself instead of a recurring $1,500-assistant chore."><summary><span class="t">Translation conveyor: a &#x27;translate&#x27; job kind for the GrowGetter ES/DE/ZH SOP</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a &#x27;translate&#x27; job kind to bridge.php that runs the already-defined SOP unattended: strip a chapter script to dialogue-only, AI-translate to ES/DE/ZH, and emit proofreader-ready packets (per-language docx + panel-reference sheet) into a handoff folder, plus a drafted Upwork message per packet (draft only, never sent). Seeder enqueues one chapter per night until the backlog clears.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> One of the 15 Magna duties goes fully automatic except the final human proofread handoff; three languages of GrowGetter back-catalog become a queue that drains itself instead of a recurring $1,500-assistant chore.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php job kinds + the documented ES/DE/ZH translation SOP + Upwork proofreader step</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="comic redactor re-release conveyor on a weekly timer a weekly cron that scans the comics.js manifest for comics older than 6 months with no re-release in a given language, runs the comic redactor fill (translated, machine-readable text in empty speech bubbles for seo), and stages a complete draft release — page images, site manifest entry, feed.xml item, and patreon/da post text — in a &#x27;staged releases&#x27; folder in studio awaiting one-click human approval. nothing publishes without the explicit ok, honoring the never-post rule. the seo re-release program (another magna duty) becomes a steady weekly drumbeat with the human role reduced to a 30-second approve click; evergreen catalog starts compounding search traffic without anyone remembering to do it."><summary><span class="t">Comic Redactor re-release conveyor on a weekly timer</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly cron that scans the comics.js manifest for comics older than 6 months with no re-release in a given language, runs the Comic Redactor fill (translated, machine-readable text in empty speech bubbles for SEO), and stages a complete draft release — page images, site manifest entry, feed.xml item, and Patreon/DA post text — in a &#x27;staged releases&#x27; folder in Studio awaiting one-click human approval. Nothing publishes without the explicit OK, honoring the never-post rule.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The SEO re-release program (another Magna duty) becomes a steady weekly drumbeat with the human role reduced to a 30-second approve click; evergreen catalog starts compounding search traffic without anyone remembering to do it.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest + Comic Redactor tool + feed.xml + the publisher stub</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="L" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="ops.php ai-owner auto-executor: the board becomes the queue a nightly job that queries ops-api.php for tasks with ownertype=ai, status open, and a filled aiplan, then spawns one headless claude code session per task (capped at ~3/night) that executes the aiplan, posts the deliverable as a board note exactly like the batch-1 pattern, and flips the status to review. tasks that fail twice get auto-flagged back to human with the error transcript attached. the command center stops being a to-do list and becomes a self-draining work queue: the ~100 ai-owned tasks from the magna transition get chipped away every single night instead of waiting for an interactive session."><summary><span class="t">ops.php AI-owner auto-executor: the board becomes the queue</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A nightly job that queries ops-api.php for tasks with ownerType=AI, status open, and a filled aiPlan, then spawns one headless Claude Code session per task (capped at ~3/night) that executes the aiPlan, posts the deliverable as a board note exactly like the Batch-1 pattern, and flips the status to review. Tasks that fail twice get auto-flagged back to Human with the error transcript attached.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The Command Center stops being a to-do list and becomes a self-draining work queue: the ~100 AI-owned tasks from the Magna transition get chipped away every single night instead of waiting for an interactive session.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> ops.php/cc.php + ownerType/aiPlan fields + Batch-1 board-note deliverable pattern + bridge.php runner</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="nightly inbox and spam sentinel with a drafts-only reply queue extend the creator pulse mac-mini sync (it already holds authenticated patreon sessions for all 4 accounts) with a nightly pass that clears spam on maxx/bloom/growgetter and pulls new patron messages/comments into a studio review queue with an ai-drafted reply attached to each — drafts only, never auto-sent, with a per-item send button for the owner or alternate. commission inquiries get auto-tagged and routed as a task on ops.php. covers three more recurring magna duties (spam, messages, commission triage) in one loop; patron response time drops from days to a next-morning batch-approve, which directly protects retention on the patreon-gated flagship."><summary><span class="t">Nightly inbox and spam sentinel with a drafts-only reply queue</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Extend the Creator Pulse Mac-mini sync (it already holds authenticated Patreon sessions for all 4 accounts) with a nightly pass that clears spam on Maxx/Bloom/GrowGetter and pulls new patron messages/comments into a Studio review queue with an AI-drafted reply attached to each — drafts only, never auto-sent, with a per-item Send button for the owner or Alternate. Commission inquiries get auto-tagged and routed as a task on ops.php.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Covers three more recurring Magna duties (spam, messages, commission triage) in one loop; patron response time drops from days to a next-morning batch-approve, which directly protects retention on the Patreon-gated flagship.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse daily sync + its 4-account Patreon sessions + ops.php task creation</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="automation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="weekly piracy sentinel that files its own board tasks a weekly cron that searches the known allporncomix forum thread plus google (site: and title-string queries for growgetter/maxx/bloom releases), diffs hits against a known-links json, and when a new leak appears files an ops.php task with the url, screenshot, and a pre-drafted dmca/takedown text. no browsing sessions, no manual checking — just a task appearing when there is something to act on. converts an easy-to-forget recurring duty into a zero-effort standing watch; new leaks of the paywalled flagship get caught in days instead of whenever someone remembers to look."><summary><span class="t">Weekly piracy sentinel that files its own board tasks</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Automation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly cron that searches the known Allporncomix forum thread plus Google (site: and title-string queries for GrowGetter/Maxx/Bloom releases), diffs hits against a known-links JSON, and when a new leak appears files an ops.php task with the URL, screenshot, and a pre-drafted DMCA/takedown text. No browsing sessions, no manual checking — just a task appearing when there is something to act on.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts an easy-to-forget recurring duty into a zero-effort standing watch; new leaks of the paywalled flagship get caught in days instead of whenever someone remembers to look.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> ops.php task API + the identified active piracy source (Allporncomix)</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="pipeline"><h3>Production <span class="n">10</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="ideator stage: corpus-mined premise engine feeding cc.php close the missing ideator stage by wiring the story-writers-room skill to real signal: mine the comic-corpus 4-axis rubric findings plus creator pulse engagement data (which growgetter/maxx/bloom posts earned the most patron response) and emit 5-10 ranked premise cards per week, each pre-scored on growth-ratio potential and stamped with a draft aiplan. cards land as tasks in cc.php with ownertype hybrid so gwhar — who loves finding and reading stories — curates winners instead of anyone inventing premises from scratch. turns &#x27;what do we make next&#x27; from an owner bottleneck into a weekly pick-from-a-menu step, and grounds every new comic in what patrons actually engaged with rather than gut feel."><summary><span class="t">Ideator stage: corpus-mined premise engine feeding cc.php</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Close the missing ideator stage by wiring the story-writers-room skill to real signal: mine the comic-corpus 4-axis rubric findings plus Creator Pulse engagement data (which GrowGetter/Maxx/Bloom posts earned the most patron response) and emit 5-10 ranked premise cards per week, each pre-scored on growth-ratio potential and stamped with a draft aiPlan. Cards land as tasks in cc.php with ownerType Hybrid so GWHAR — who loves finding and reading stories — curates winners instead of anyone inventing premises from scratch.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns &#x27;what do we make next&#x27; from an owner bottleneck into a weekly pick-from-a-menu step, and grounds every new comic in what patrons actually engaged with rather than gut feel.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> story-writers-room skill, comic-corpus rubric, Creator Pulse, cc.php Command Center</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="writer stage: lesson-compliant script generator emitting shotlist format add a comic-writer skill to claude-comic-pipeline that takes a picked premise card and outputs a full script with the 35 lessons pre-baked as constraints (growth density mandate, expression intensity per beat, camera dynamism, wardrobe locks, hair-state anchors) — emitted directly in script-breakdown&#x27;s shotlist schema so it flows straight into generation with zero reformatting. same skill covers two magna duties in the recurring-15 list: weekly/monthly artist scripts for bloom+maxx and fan art friday scripts. closes the writer gap and absorbs three recurring magna duties in one build; scripts arrive generation-ready, so premise-to-panels drops from days of manual scripting to one command."><summary><span class="t">Writer stage: lesson-compliant script generator emitting shotlist format</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a comic-writer skill to claude-comic-pipeline that takes a picked premise card and outputs a full script with the 35 lessons pre-baked as constraints (growth density mandate, expression intensity per beat, camera dynamism, wardrobe locks, hair-state anchors) — emitted directly in script-breakdown&#x27;s shotlist schema so it flows straight into generation with zero reformatting. Same skill covers two Magna duties in the recurring-15 list: weekly/monthly artist scripts for Bloom+Maxx and Fan Art Friday scripts.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Closes the writer gap and absorbs three recurring Magna duties in one build; scripts arrive generation-ready, so premise-to-panels drops from days of manual scripting to one command.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> claude-comic-pipeline (script-breakdown, comic-production 35 lessons)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="translation factory: one-command growgetter es/de/zh chapter pipeline industrialize the translation sop as a bridge.php job kind &#x27;translate&#x27;: extract dialogue using import.php&#x27;s existing ai dialogue-read machinery, machine-translate against a persistent glossary (character names, sfx conventions, growth terminology so &#x27;huge&#x27; beats stay consistent), re-letter pages via page-composer, and emit a proofreader packet (side-by-side en/target doc) ready to hand to the upwork proofreaders. one command per chapter per language, tracked as a job with heartbeat/done like any other worker job. collapses the multi-step manual sop (strip, translate, send, re-letter) into a single queued job, unlocking a 3x content multiplier on the flagship at near-zero marginal effort — only proofreading stays human."><summary><span class="t">Translation factory: one-command GrowGetter ES/DE/ZH chapter pipeline</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Industrialize the translation SOP as a bridge.php job kind &#x27;translate&#x27;: extract dialogue using import.php&#x27;s existing AI dialogue-read machinery, machine-translate against a persistent glossary (character names, SFX conventions, growth terminology so &#x27;HUGE&#x27; beats stay consistent), re-letter pages via page-composer, and emit a proofreader packet (side-by-side EN/target doc) ready to hand to the Upwork proofreaders. One command per chapter per language, tracked as a job with heartbeat/done like any other worker job.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Collapses the multi-step manual SOP (strip, translate, send, re-letter) into a single queued job, unlocking a 3x content multiplier on the flagship at near-zero marginal effort — only proofreading stays human.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php worker protocol, import.php dialogue read, page-composer skill</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="comic redactor conveyor: auto-queued &gt;6-month re-release batches automate the redactor duty end-to-end: a monthly job crawls the comics.js manifest for comics older than 6 months, runs each through the translate pipeline above plus seo speech-bubble fill (machine-readable text in empty bubbles, per the existing redactor concept), and stages complete re-release packages in a queue. alternate&#x27;s only job is pressing publish on each staged package — no selection, prep, or lettering work. converts a dormant back-catalog into a steady seo and re-engagement drip; a duty that consumed magna hours becomes a monthly cron plus one human click per release."><summary><span class="t">Comic Redactor conveyor: auto-queued &gt;6-month re-release batches</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Automate the Redactor duty end-to-end: a monthly job crawls the comics.js manifest for comics older than 6 months, runs each through the translate pipeline above plus SEO speech-bubble fill (machine-readable text in empty bubbles, per the existing Redactor concept), and stages complete re-release packages in a queue. Alternate&#x27;s only job is pressing publish on each staged package — no selection, prep, or lettering work.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts a dormant back-catalog into a steady SEO and re-engagement drip; a duty that consumed Magna hours becomes a monthly cron plus one human click per release.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest, translation pipeline, import.php, Comic Redactor concept from the recurring-duties list</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="pre-flight genspec linter: 35 lessons enforced before generation, not after turn the codified failure-mode lessons into a mechanical lint pass inside bridge.php&#x27;s genspec step: before a worker claims a job, check the prompt for lesson compliance (hair state named when head in frame, 5+ env anchor elements, wardrobe lock present, accessory suppression, no anatomy keywords that trigger wardrobe drift, refs attached not described) and auto-patch or bounce non-compliant specs. this moves the existing qa gate chain from post-gen detection to pre-gen prevention. directly raises first-pass keep rate and cuts higgsfield credit burn and flow retries — every defect caught pre-gen is a paid generation not wasted."><summary><span class="t">Pre-flight genspec linter: 35 lessons enforced before generation, not after</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Turn the codified failure-mode lessons into a mechanical lint pass inside bridge.php&#x27;s genspec step: before a worker claims a job, check the prompt for lesson compliance (hair state named when head in frame, 5+ env anchor elements, wardrobe lock present, accessory suppression, no anatomy keywords that trigger wardrobe drift, refs attached not described) and auto-patch or bounce non-compliant specs. This moves the existing QA gate chain from post-gen detection to pre-gen prevention.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Directly raises first-pass keep rate and cuts Higgsfield credit burn and Flow retries — every defect caught pre-gen is a paid generation not wasted.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php genspec, comic-production 35 lessons, creator.php ck_ai_qa scan</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="keep/trash telemetry: learn which prompt patterns actually land log every generation&#x27;s prompt features (model, ref count, camera angle, lesson-compliance flags, i2i vs t2i, source-anchor presence) alongside its keep/trash verdict from the existing keyboard-rating loop and qa scan into a stats table in studio. a weekly auto-report surfaces which patterns burn credits and which hit, and the findings feed thresholds back into the pre-flight linter. converts the already-happening rating clicks into a compounding dataset; within a few weeks you get empirical, per-model hit-rate numbers instead of anecdotes, steering credit spend toward what works."><summary><span class="t">Keep/trash telemetry: learn which prompt patterns actually land</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Log every generation&#x27;s prompt features (model, ref count, camera angle, lesson-compliance flags, i2i vs t2i, source-anchor presence) alongside its keep/trash verdict from the existing keyboard-rating loop and QA scan into a stats table in Studio. A weekly auto-report surfaces which patterns burn credits and which hit, and the findings feed thresholds back into the pre-flight linter.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts the already-happening rating clicks into a compounding dataset; within a few weeks you get empirical, per-model hit-rate numbers instead of anecdotes, steering credit spend toward what works.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> creator.php rating loop, ck_ai_qa, flow-studio-autosync ingest</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="auto-trailer per release: productize the seedance comic-to-clip pipeline codify the proven müller 02 workflow (47 panels to 18 clips) as a &#x27;trailer&#x27; bridge.php job: auto-pick the top 4-6 growth panels of a finished chapter using the corpus growth-ratio detector, animate them seedance mini @480p, and ffmpeg-cut a 30-60s vertical teaser with title card and cta. every published comic ships with a promo clip staged for patreon/da/discord; standout chapters get a std-quality upgrade pass as a paid video product. every release gets motion marketing for ~60-90 credits of mini generations, and the same pipeline seeds video-as-a-product (animated editions) with no new r&amp;d."><summary><span class="t">Auto-trailer per release: productize the Seedance comic-to-clip pipeline</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Codify the proven Müller 02 workflow (47 panels to 18 clips) as a &#x27;trailer&#x27; bridge.php job: auto-pick the top 4-6 growth panels of a finished chapter using the corpus growth-ratio detector, animate them Seedance mini @480p, and ffmpeg-cut a 30-60s vertical teaser with title card and CTA. Every published comic ships with a promo clip staged for Patreon/DA/Discord; standout chapters get a std-quality upgrade pass as a paid video product.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Every release gets motion marketing for ~60-90 credits of mini generations, and the same pipeline seeds video-as-a-product (animated editions) with no new R&amp;D.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Seedance video pipeline + Müller 02 shotlist method, bridge.php, comic-corpus growth-ratio rubric</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="publisher stage: release-kit packager with human-press-go queue replace the publisher stub with studio/publish.php: given a finished chapter, generate the complete publish kit — comics.js manifest entry + feed.xml item for the custom site, patreon post draft per account, da description with tags, discord announcement — all staged as drafts with one &#x27;post&#x27; button per destination. alternate works the queue; nothing goes out without a human click, honoring the no-posting-without-permission rule by design. publishing a chapter drops from an hour of copy-writing and tab-juggling across 6+ destinations to five minutes of review clicks, and makes alternate immediately productive with zero training."><summary><span class="t">Publisher stage: release-kit packager with human-press-go queue</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Replace the publisher stub with studio/publish.php: given a finished chapter, generate the complete publish kit — comics.js manifest entry + feed.xml item for the custom site, Patreon post draft per account, DA description with tags, Discord announcement — all staged as drafts with one &#x27;post&#x27; button per destination. Alternate works the queue; nothing goes out without a human click, honoring the no-posting-without-permission rule by design.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Publishing a chapter drops from an hour of copy-writing and tab-juggling across 6+ destinations to five minutes of review clicks, and makes Alternate immediately productive with zero training.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Studio PHP (new publish.php), comics.js/feed.xml CMS, ops.php task board</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="overnight drain: nightly runner that empties the bridge.php job queue formalize the always-on runner concept, scoped to content jobs only: a nightly cron on the mac mini (which already runs the creator pulse daily sync) starts a worker that drains whatever is queued in bridge.php — transforms, translations, redactor batches, trailer renders — using the proven autonomous 44-panel overnight protocol, then posts a morning summary with pass/fail counts and qa flags to ops.php. makes the recent overnight-autonomy win the default operating mode: the queue empties while the owner sleeps, and mornings start with a triage summary instead of a backlog."><summary><span class="t">Overnight drain: nightly runner that empties the bridge.php job queue</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Formalize the always-on runner concept, scoped to content jobs only: a nightly cron on the Mac mini (which already runs the Creator Pulse daily sync) starts a worker that drains whatever is queued in bridge.php — transforms, translations, Redactor batches, trailer renders — using the proven autonomous 44-panel overnight protocol, then posts a morning summary with pass/fail counts and QA flags to ops.php.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Makes the recent overnight-autonomy win the default operating mode: the queue empties while the owner sleeps, and mornings start with a triage summary instead of a backlog.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php claim/heartbeat/done protocol, Mac mini daily-sync host, autonomous 44-panel run, ops.php</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="pipeline" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="fan art friday picker: patron-signal character selection plus pitch cards automate the two faf duties from the magna list: scan patreon comments/messages and patron suggestions via the creator pulse data path, rank candidate patron characters by recency and engagement, and emit 3 pitch cards (character, one-line premise, draft character lock per the vivid-locks rule). gwhar or the owner picks one; the comic-writer skill then produces the faf script automatically. two recurring weekly duties shrink to a single pick-one-of-three decision, and choices become defensible with engagement data — patrons see their actual requests get made."><summary><span class="t">Fan Art Friday picker: patron-signal character selection plus pitch cards</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Production</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Automate the two FAF duties from the Magna list: scan Patreon comments/messages and patron suggestions via the Creator Pulse data path, rank candidate patron characters by recency and engagement, and emit 3 pitch cards (character, one-line premise, draft character lock per the vivid-locks rule). GWHAR or the owner picks one; the comic-writer skill then produces the FAF script automatically.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Two recurring weekly duties shrink to a single pick-one-of-three decision, and choices become defensible with engagement data — patrons see their actual requests get made.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse Patreon sync, comic-writer skill (idea 2), character-lock conventions</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="distribution"><h3>Distribution <span class="n">9</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="syndicator v1: publish.php fires a per-channel posting queue with a studio/syndicate.php cockpit for alternate when a comic goes live, publish.php writes a syndication queue entry per channel (deviantart, twitter, discord, free-patreon teaser) into a queue json the same way bridge.php stores jobs. a new studio/syndicate.php page shows alternate ready-to-post packages: pre-cropped images per channel&#x27;s aspect ratio, ai-written caption + hashtags generated at publish time, and a utm-tagged link. alternate posts manually, clicks &#x27;mark posted&#x27;, and pastes the live url back — which feeds attribution.php so every channel post becomes a tracked touchpoint. human stays on the submit button, satisfying the never-post-without-permission rule. turns &#x27;share on socials&#x27; from a magna duty into a 5-minute-per-release checklist a $100/mo helper can run; every post becomes attributable in the v5 cockpit so the owner finally learns which channel converts to patreon."><summary><span class="t">Syndicator v1: publish.php fires a per-channel posting queue with a studio/syndicate.php cockpit for Alternate</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>When a comic goes live, publish.php writes a syndication queue entry per channel (DeviantArt, Twitter, Discord, free-Patreon teaser) into a queue JSON the same way bridge.php stores jobs. A new studio/syndicate.php page shows Alternate ready-to-post packages: pre-cropped images per channel&#x27;s aspect ratio, AI-written caption + hashtags generated at publish time, and a UTM-tagged link. Alternate posts manually, clicks &#x27;mark posted&#x27;, and pastes the live URL back — which feeds attribution.php so every channel post becomes a tracked touchpoint. Human stays on the submit button, satisfying the never-post-without-permission rule.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns &#x27;share on socials&#x27; from a Magna duty into a 5-minute-per-release checklist a $100/mo helper can run; every post becomes attributable in the v5 cockpit so the owner finally learns which channel converts to Patreon.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> publish.php stub, bridge.php queue pattern, attribution.php ATS v5, ops ownership layer (Alternate=posting)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="auto-generated og/twitter share cards injected at deploy time add a tools/make-sharecards.sh step to deploy_3dmc.sh that, for every entry in comics.js, composites the cover panel + logo + title into a 1200x630 og image (page-composer skill already does exactly this kind of compositing) and injects og:image/og:title/og:description/twitter:card meta tags into each comic&#x27;s static page. backfill the whole catalog in one run. every link alternate drops on discord/da/twitter/patreon unfurls as a big compelling panel instead of a bare url — the single cheapest ctr multiplier available, and it makes all downstream syndication work harder-hitting for free."><summary><span class="t">Auto-generated OG/Twitter share cards injected at deploy time</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a tools/make-sharecards.sh step to deploy_3dmc.sh that, for every entry in comics.js, composites the cover panel + logo + title into a 1200x630 OG image (page-composer skill already does exactly this kind of compositing) and injects og:image/og:title/og:description/twitter:card meta tags into each comic&#x27;s static page. Backfill the whole catalog in one run.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Every link Alternate drops on Discord/DA/Twitter/Patreon unfurls as a big compelling panel instead of a bare URL — the single cheapest CTR multiplier available, and it makes all downstream syndication work harder-hitting for free.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest, tools/deploy_3dmc.sh, page-composer compositing</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="discord webhook autopost on publish + weekly &#x27;from the vault&#x27; repost cron discord is an owned channel where a standing webhook is safe and trivial: publish.php posts the cover image, title, blurb, and utm&#x27;d site link to a discord webhook on every release. add a weekly cron (on the mac mini next to the creator pulse daily sync) that picks a &gt;1-year-old comic from comics.js and posts it as a throwback. owner approves the webhook setup once. discord becomes a fully hands-off channel with 2+ touchpoints/week instead of relying on anyone remembering to post; the vault reposts resurface back-catalog to members who joined after those comics dropped."><summary><span class="t">Discord webhook autopost on publish + weekly &#x27;from the vault&#x27; repost cron</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Discord is an owned channel where a standing webhook is safe and trivial: publish.php POSTs the cover image, title, blurb, and UTM&#x27;d site link to a Discord webhook on every release. Add a weekly cron (on the Mac mini next to the Creator Pulse daily sync) that picks a &gt;1-year-old comic from comics.js and posts it as a throwback. Owner approves the webhook setup once.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Discord becomes a fully hands-off channel with 2+ touchpoints/week instead of relying on anyone remembering to post; the vault reposts resurface back-catalog to members who joined after those comics dropped.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> publish.php, comics.js, Mac mini cron alongside Creator Pulse sync</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="crawlable transcript + json-ld + sitemap layer for every comic page the import.php dialogue-reader already extracts speech-bubble text from comic pages with ai. run it across the whole catalog once to produce an english transcript per comic, and have the deploy script inject it as a collapsible &#x27;transcript&#x27; block plus image alt text and comicissue/comicseries json-ld on each comic page, and generate sitemap.xml from comics.js. right now the site is image-only pages google can barely index. the entire back catalog becomes text-searchable to google overnight — long-tail queries like character names and story beats start landing on 3dmusclecomics.com instead of pirate forums, at zero ongoing cost."><summary><span class="t">Crawlable transcript + JSON-LD + sitemap layer for every comic page</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The import.php dialogue-reader already extracts speech-bubble text from comic pages with AI. Run it across the whole catalog once to produce an English transcript per comic, and have the deploy script inject it as a collapsible &#x27;transcript&#x27; block plus image alt text and ComicIssue/ComicSeries JSON-LD on each comic page, and generate sitemap.xml from comics.js. Right now the site is image-only pages Google can barely index.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The entire back catalog becomes text-searchable to Google overnight — long-tail queries like character names and story beats start landing on 3dmusclecomics.com instead of pirate forums, at zero ongoing cost.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> import.php AI dialogue-read step, comics.js, deploy_3dmc.sh, feed.xml</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="L" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="comic redactor engine: studio/redactor.php for multilingual back-catalog re-releases the redactor duty (re-release &gt;6-month-old comics translated, with machine-readable bubble text) has no tooling yet. build studio/redactor.php as an import.php sibling: pick an old comic from comics.js → dialogue-read extracts the script → ai translates to es/de/zh per the existing strip-to-dialogue sop → page-composer re-letters pages → output lands in the draft organizer for the existing upwork-proofreader pass → publish as /es/ /de/ /zh/ pages with hreflang tags and their own feed entries. converts a dormant magna duty into a repeatable pipeline that roughly triples the indexable catalog across three languages — each re-release is &#x27;new&#x27; seo content and a fresh syndication package without generating a single new panel."><summary><span class="t">Comic Redactor engine: studio/redactor.php for multilingual back-catalog re-releases</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The Redactor duty (re-release &gt;6-month-old comics translated, with machine-readable bubble text) has no tooling yet. Build studio/redactor.php as an import.php sibling: pick an old comic from comics.js → dialogue-read extracts the script → AI translates to ES/DE/ZH per the existing strip-to-dialogue SOP → page-composer re-letters pages → output lands in the draft organizer for the existing Upwork-proofreader pass → publish as /es/ /de/ /zh/ pages with hreflang tags and their own feed entries.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts a dormant Magna duty into a repeatable pipeline that roughly triples the indexable catalog across three languages — each re-release is &#x27;new&#x27; SEO content and a fresh syndication package without generating a single new panel.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> import.php dialogue reader, page-composer lettering, translation SOP + Upwork proofreaders, comics.js, studio draft organizer</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="public growgetter teaser pages with utm&#x27;d patreon ctas — measurable free-to-paid funnel at publish time, auto-build a public teaser page on 3dmusclecomics.com for each patreon-gated growgetter chapter: first 3-4 pages pulled from the studio draft organizer, a cliffhanger crop of the moment before the biggest growth beat, and a patreon button carrying utm parameters that attribution.php already tracks. the syndication queue links to the teaser page, never the raw paywall. gives every social post a landing page that converts instead of a paywall dead-end, and closes the attribution loop so the owner can see teaser-view-to-pledge conversion per channel for the flagship property."><summary><span class="t">Public GrowGetter teaser pages with UTM&#x27;d Patreon CTAs — measurable free-to-paid funnel</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>At publish time, auto-build a public teaser page on 3dmusclecomics.com for each Patreon-gated GrowGetter chapter: first 3-4 pages pulled from the studio draft organizer, a cliffhanger crop of the moment before the biggest growth beat, and a Patreon button carrying UTM parameters that attribution.php already tracks. The syndication queue links to the teaser page, never the raw paywall.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Gives every social post a landing page that converts instead of a paywall dead-end, and closes the attribution loop so the owner can see teaser-view-to-pledge conversion per channel for the flagship property.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> studio draft organizer, publish.php, attribution.php ATS v5, static-site deploy</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="da-post-helper chrome extension that prefills submissions from the syndication queue a fourth chrome extension in the established pattern (flow-studio-autosync, patreon downloader, flow bulk downloader): it reads the pending deviantart entry from bridge.php, and when alternate opens da&#x27;s submit page it prefills title, description, tags, and mature-content flags and attaches the image — alternate reviews and clicks submit personally. on success it reports the live url back to bridge.php, closing the queue item automatically. cuts da posting from ~10 minutes of copy-paste per submission to under 1, across 4 properties — which is the difference between alternate actually keeping a consistent da cadence and it quietly lapsing. the same skeleton later extends to twitter/ig."><summary><span class="t">DA-post-helper Chrome extension that prefills submissions from the syndication queue</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A fourth Chrome extension in the established pattern (flow-studio-autosync, Patreon downloader, Flow bulk downloader): it reads the pending DeviantArt entry from bridge.php, and when Alternate opens DA&#x27;s submit page it prefills title, description, tags, and mature-content flags and attaches the image — Alternate reviews and clicks Submit personally. On success it reports the live URL back to bridge.php, closing the queue item automatically.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Cuts DA posting from ~10 minutes of copy-paste per submission to under 1, across 4 properties — which is the difference between Alternate actually keeping a consistent DA cadence and it quietly lapsing. The same skeleton later extends to Twitter/IG.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php protocol, flow-studio-autosync extension architecture, syndication queue (idea 1)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="weekly piracy-watch cron that files pre-drafted dmca tasks into ops.php, plus watermark footers on free pages a weekly scheduled agent searches for each comic title + distinctive dialogue strings (now available from the transcript layer) across google and the known pirate venues including the active allporncomix thread, diffs hits against a known-list, and creates an ops.php task per new hit with a pre-drafted dmca notice in the aiplan field — owner just reviews and sends. separately, add a one-line page-composer export option stamping a small 3dmusclecomics.com footer on all freely-distributed pages. piracy monitoring goes from an unstaffed magna duty to a 5-minute weekly review, and every pirated copy that does escape carries the site url — converting leakage into top-of-funnel traffic."><summary><span class="t">Weekly piracy-watch cron that files pre-drafted DMCA tasks into ops.php, plus watermark footers on free pages</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly scheduled agent searches for each comic title + distinctive dialogue strings (now available from the transcript layer) across Google and the known pirate venues including the active Allporncomix thread, diffs hits against a known-list, and creates an ops.php task per new hit with a pre-drafted DMCA notice in the aiPlan field — owner just reviews and sends. Separately, add a one-line page-composer export option stamping a small 3dmusclecomics.com footer on all freely-distributed pages.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Piracy monitoring goes from an unstaffed Magna duty to a 5-minute weekly review, and every pirated copy that does escape carries the site URL — converting leakage into top-of-funnel traffic.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> ops.php aiPlan fields, scheduled-tasks/Mac mini cron, page-composer export, transcript layer (idea 4)</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="distribution" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="fan art friday as the weekly public content engine, driven by gwhar repoint the faf duty into a discovery machine: gwhar (who loves characters and reading stories) picks the patron character in ops.php, a growgetter.php-style one-click generator produces a sfw single-page comic through the existing worker/bridge pipeline with the qa defect scan, and the result drops into the syndication queue for alternate to post publicly on da/twitter/discord with the patron credited. owner approves each before it queues. guarantees a 52-posts-a-year public cadence of shareable sfw content — the consistent free output all four social channels currently lack — while making patrons the stars, which is the strongest organic-share and retention lever the operation has."><summary><span class="t">Fan Art Friday as the weekly public content engine, driven by GWHAR</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Distribution</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Repoint the FAF duty into a discovery machine: GWHAR (who loves characters and reading stories) picks the patron character in ops.php, a growgetter.php-style one-click generator produces a SFW single-page comic through the existing worker/bridge pipeline with the QA defect scan, and the result drops into the syndication queue for Alternate to post publicly on DA/Twitter/Discord with the patron credited. Owner approves each before it queues.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Guarantees a 52-posts-a-year public cadence of shareable SFW content — the consistent free output all four social channels currently lack — while making patrons the stars, which is the strongest organic-share and retention lever the operation has.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> growgetter.php one-click generator, bridge.php worker protocol, creator.php AI QA scan, ops.php ownership layer (GWHAR=content), syndication queue (idea 1)</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="revenue"><h3>Patrons &amp; Revenue <span class="n">9</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="fan art friday autopilot: submission backlog → poll → ai script → generation queue add a studio/faf.php section that holds the patron character-submission backlog per property. gwhar (who loves characters) curates 4-6 candidates monthly; the tool emits a ready-to-paste patreon poll; when the winner is in, the ai writes the faf script with the comic-production skill and files a genspec job into bridge.php so the overnight worker renders it — same protocol the 44-panel autonomous run proved. alternate posts the result; owner never touches it except veto. eliminates two of magna&#x27;s 15 recurring duties outright (pick faf characters, write faf scripts) and turns faf from a chore into a reliable weekly patron-retention ritual — poll participation itself is an engagement/retention lever on all 4 patreons."><summary><span class="t">Fan Art Friday Autopilot: submission backlog → poll → AI script → generation queue</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a studio/faf.php section that holds the patron character-submission backlog per property. GWHAR (who loves characters) curates 4-6 candidates monthly; the tool emits a ready-to-paste Patreon poll; when the winner is in, the AI writes the FAF script with the comic-production skill and files a genspec job into bridge.php so the overnight worker renders it — same protocol the 44-panel autonomous run proved. Alternate posts the result; owner never touches it except veto.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Eliminates two of Magna&#x27;s 15 recurring duties outright (pick FAF characters, write FAF scripts) and turns FAF from a chore into a reliable weekly patron-retention ritual — poll participation itself is an engagement/retention lever on all 4 Patreons.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php worker protocol, comic-production skill, ops.php duty board</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="patreon reply queue: ai-drafted answers, one-click human send extend the creator pulse daily sync on the mac mini (already authenticated to all 4 patreon accounts) to also pull unread messages and comments into a studio/inbox.php queue. ai drafts a reply per item in the owner&#x27;s voice, few-shot from past replies, tagged by type (thanks, request, complaint, commission inquiry). owner or alternate reviews and clicks send — nothing ever auto-sends, matching the standing no-post-without-permission rule. removes &#x27;answer patreon messages/comments&#x27; from the magna duty list and cuts reply time from minutes each to seconds each; faster replies are one of the strongest cheap retention levers on patreon. becomes the delivery rail for ideas 3, 4, and 6 below."><summary><span class="t">Patreon reply queue: AI-drafted answers, one-click human send</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Extend the Creator Pulse daily sync on the Mac mini (already authenticated to all 4 Patreon accounts) to also pull unread messages and comments into a studio/inbox.php queue. AI drafts a reply per item in the owner&#x27;s voice, few-shot from past replies, tagged by type (thanks, request, complaint, commission inquiry). Owner or Alternate reviews and clicks send — nothing ever auto-sends, matching the standing no-post-without-permission rule.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Removes &#x27;answer Patreon messages/comments&#x27; from the Magna duty list and cuts reply time from minutes each to seconds each; faster replies are one of the strongest cheap retention levers on Patreon. Becomes the delivery rail for ideas 3, 4, and 6 below.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse Mac mini daily sync, Studio PHP shell</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="churn early-warning list in creator pulse with drafted win-back dms add an &#x27;at risk&#x27; panel to creator pulse&#x27;s 4-account rollup: flag patrons who downgraded, scheduled a cancel, had a declined payment, or went engagement-silent for 60+ days after prior activity. for each, ai drafts a short personal dm referencing the specific comics they engaged with (data pulse already has) and pushes it into the inbox.php approval queue. turns pulse from a rear-view dashboard into a revenue-defense tool; recovering even 2-3 churning growgetter patrons a month likely pays for gwhar&#x27;s entire salary. declined-payment nudges alone typically recover a meaningful slice of involuntary churn."><summary><span class="t">Churn early-warning list in Creator Pulse with drafted win-back DMs</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add an &#x27;At Risk&#x27; panel to Creator Pulse&#x27;s 4-account rollup: flag patrons who downgraded, scheduled a cancel, had a declined payment, or went engagement-silent for 60+ days after prior activity. For each, AI drafts a short personal DM referencing the specific comics they engaged with (data Pulse already has) and pushes it into the inbox.php approval queue.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns Pulse from a rear-view dashboard into a revenue-defense tool; recovering even 2-3 churning GrowGetter patrons a month likely pays for GWHAR&#x27;s entire salary. Declined-payment nudges alone typically recover a meaningful slice of involuntary churn.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse rollup + daily sync, inbox.php reply queue</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="new-patron welcome dm sequence the creator pulse sync already sees new pledges daily. on each new patron, auto-draft a tier-aware welcome dm into the reply queue: best-of comics for their tier, how to submit a character for fan art friday, and the commission link. one template per property, personalized with name and tier, human-approved before send. first-30-day churn is where patreon loses most patrons; a personal welcome measurably improves early retention and immediately advertises the faf and commission revenue paths. near-zero marginal work once built."><summary><span class="t">New-patron welcome DM sequence</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The Creator Pulse sync already sees new pledges daily. On each new patron, auto-draft a tier-aware welcome DM into the reply queue: best-of comics for their tier, how to submit a character for Fan Art Friday, and the commission link. One template per property, personalized with name and tier, human-approved before send.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> First-30-day churn is where Patreon loses most patrons; a personal welcome measurably improves early retention and immediately advertises the FAF and commission revenue paths. Near-zero marginal work once built.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse new-pledge detection, inbox.php reply queue</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="spam sweeper: nightly flag, batch review, one click to clear a nightly job on the mac mini scans comments/messages across maxx, bloom, and growgetter via the existing pulse sessions, scores likely spam (link patterns, known spam phrasing, zero-pledge accounts), and builds a single review screen — same pattern as the review-composite-before-trash workflow. alternate or the owner approves the batch and executes the deletions themselves. removes the &#x27;clear spam&#x27; magna duty and shrinks it from a recurring multi-account slog to a 60-second daily review. also keeps comment sections clean, which patrons notice."><summary><span class="t">Spam sweeper: nightly flag, batch review, one click to clear</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A nightly job on the Mac mini scans comments/messages across Maxx, Bloom, and GrowGetter via the existing Pulse sessions, scores likely spam (link patterns, known spam phrasing, zero-pledge accounts), and builds a single review screen — same pattern as the review-composite-before-trash workflow. Alternate or the owner approves the batch and executes the deletions themselves.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Removes the &#x27;clear spam&#x27; Magna duty and shrinks it from a recurring multi-account slog to a 60-second daily review. Also keeps comment sections clean, which patrons notice.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse authenticated sessions, review-composite approval pattern</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="commission intake funnel: structured form → ops.php card → drafted quote add a /commissions page to 3dmusclecomics.com (via the existing php cms admin) with a structured brief form: character refs upload, growth flavor, size stage, page count, budget band, deadline. submissions land as ops.php cards with the aiplan field pre-filled (&#x27;how ai would produce this&#x27;), and ai drafts the quote/scope reply into the inbox.php queue for approval. replaces the ad-hoc &#x27;discuss commissions&#x27; dm back-and-forth duty with a funnel that qualifies buyers before any human time is spent, and since the autonomous transform run proved unattended production, commission margin goes way up — most of the fulfillment cost is now electricity."><summary><span class="t">Commission intake funnel: structured form → ops.php card → drafted quote</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a /commissions page to 3dmusclecomics.com (via the existing PHP CMS admin) with a structured brief form: character refs upload, growth flavor, size stage, page count, budget band, deadline. Submissions land as ops.php cards with the aiPlan field pre-filled (&#x27;how AI would produce this&#x27;), and AI drafts the quote/scope reply into the inbox.php queue for approval.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Replaces the ad-hoc &#x27;discuss commissions&#x27; DM back-and-forth duty with a funnel that qualifies buyers before any human time is spent, and since the autonomous transform run proved unattended production, commission margin goes way up — most of the fulfillment cost is now electricity.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> 3dmusclecomics.com PHP CMS, ops.php board with aiPlan field, inbox.php</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="cross-patreon teaser syndicator: every release drafts promos for the other three accounts watch comics.js/feed.xml for new publishes; on each, use page-composer to assemble a sfw 3-panel teaser page from existing panels with a &#x27;read the full comic on [property]&#x27; caption, and drop ready-to-post drafts (image + copy) into a per-account folder for alternate to post on the other three patreons plus deviantart. nothing posts automatically. the 4 patreons currently barely feed each other; systematic cross-promotion is the cheapest patron-acquisition channel available since the audiences already trust the brand. also gives alternate a clear, zero-judgment posting queue."><summary><span class="t">Cross-Patreon teaser syndicator: every release drafts promos for the other three accounts</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Watch comics.js/feed.xml for new publishes; on each, use page-composer to assemble a SFW 3-panel teaser page from existing panels with a &#x27;read the full comic on [property]&#x27; caption, and drop ready-to-post drafts (image + copy) into a per-account folder for Alternate to post on the other three Patreons plus DeviantArt. Nothing posts automatically.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The 4 Patreons currently barely feed each other; systematic cross-promotion is the cheapest patron-acquisition channel available since the audiences already trust the brand. Also gives Alternate a clear, zero-judgment posting queue.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> comics.js manifest + feed.xml, page-composer skill, Alternate posting role</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="vault tier pilot: monetize comic redactor re-releases as a low-price back-catalog tier use creator pulse engagement data to pick growgetter&#x27;s 10 highest-engagement comics older than 6 months, run them through the comic redactor re-release flow, and launch a cheap &#x27;vault&#x27; archive tier on one account as a 60-day experiment (price point owner-chosen, e.g. $3-5). pulse already measures the outcome: net new patrons, upgrades, cannibalization of existing tiers. first real pricing experiment with a built-in measurement loop, and it turns the redactor seo chore into a direct revenue product. back-catalog tiers convert lurkers who balk at flagship pricing."><summary><span class="t">Vault tier pilot: monetize Comic Redactor re-releases as a low-price back-catalog tier</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Use Creator Pulse engagement data to pick GrowGetter&#x27;s 10 highest-engagement comics older than 6 months, run them through the Comic Redactor re-release flow, and launch a cheap &#x27;Vault&#x27; archive tier on ONE account as a 60-day experiment (price point owner-chosen, e.g. $3-5). Pulse already measures the outcome: net new patrons, upgrades, cannibalization of existing tiers.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> First real pricing experiment with a built-in measurement loop, and it turns the Redactor SEO chore into a direct revenue product. Back-catalog tiers convert lurkers who balk at flagship pricing.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Comic Redactor re-release duty, Creator Pulse analytics</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="revenue" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="monthly patron story polls that seed the missing ideator stage once a month per property, run the story-writers-room skill locally to generate 4 competing one-line premises with storyboard thumbnails; alternate posts them as a patreon image poll. the winning premise becomes an ops.php card tagged as the next monthly comic brief — patron votes literally feed the &#x27;ideator&#x27; gap in the 7-stage assembly line. patrons who voted for a comic stick around to see it made — polls double as a retention mechanic and a churn-proof content roadmap, while closing the top of the assembly line with almost no owner judgment required."><summary><span class="t">Monthly patron story polls that seed the missing ideator stage</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Patrons &amp; Revenue</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Once a month per property, run the story-writers-room skill locally to generate 4 competing one-line premises with storyboard thumbnails; Alternate posts them as a Patreon image poll. The winning premise becomes an ops.php card tagged as the next monthly comic brief — patron votes literally feed the &#x27;ideator&#x27; gap in the 7-stage assembly line.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Patrons who voted for a comic stick around to see it made — polls double as a retention mechanic and a churn-proof content roadmap, while closing the top of the assembly line with almost no owner judgment required.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> story-writers-room skill, ops.php/cc.php board, Alternate posting role</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="delegation"><h3>Delegation <span class="n">10</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="magna exit-brain-dump sprint (sop capture before he&#x27;s gone) this week, while magna is still reachable, send him a templated questionnaire + screen-recording request for each of the 15 recurring duties: exact steps, logins/urls touched, cadence, edge cases, &#x27;what goes wrong&#x27;. ai transcribes each recording and converts it into a per-duty sop markdown committed to the claude-comic-pipeline repo, and pastes the sop link into that duty&#x27;s aiplan field on cc.php so the assignee (gwhar/alternate/ai) inherits the knowledge, not just the task. prevents irreversible knowledge loss — once he leaves, reconstructing &#x27;how do sketches get shared across 4 patreons&#x27; costs days of trial and error. every downstream routing idea gets cheaper because the sop exists."><summary><span class="t">Magna exit-brain-dump sprint (SOP capture before he&#x27;s gone)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>This week, while Magna is still reachable, send him a templated questionnaire + screen-recording request for each of the 15 recurring duties: exact steps, logins/URLs touched, cadence, edge cases, &#x27;what goes wrong&#x27;. AI transcribes each recording and converts it into a per-duty SOP markdown committed to the claude-comic-pipeline repo, and pastes the SOP link into that duty&#x27;s aiPlan field on cc.php so the assignee (GWHAR/Alternate/AI) inherits the knowledge, not just the task.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Prevents irreversible knowledge loss — once he leaves, reconstructing &#x27;how do sketches get shared across 4 Patreons&#x27; costs days of trial and error. Every downstream routing idea gets cheaper because the SOP exists.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> cc.php aiPlan field + claude-comic-pipeline repo</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="per-person queue views on the command center (gwhar + alternate logins) extend ops.php/cc.php with two more studio logins (the magnamus studio-only login pattern already exists) and a filtered &#x27;my queue&#x27; view: each person sees only tasks where assignee=them, sorted by due date, with a done button and a notes box. add a ?me= view so gwhar and alternate never see the 388-task firehose or each other&#x27;s pay-sensitive items. turns the ownership-layer triage (already started) into something the two humans can actually work from without the owner relaying tasks over discord daily. delegation stops being a chat thread."><summary><span class="t">Per-person queue views on the Command Center (GWHAR + Alternate logins)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Extend ops.php/cc.php with two more studio logins (the Magnamus studio-only login pattern already exists) and a filtered &#x27;my queue&#x27; view: each person sees only tasks where assignee=them, sorted by due date, with a Done button and a notes box. Add a ?me= view so GWHAR and Alternate never see the 388-task firehose or each other&#x27;s pay-sensitive items.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns the ownership-layer triage (already started) into something the two humans can actually work from without the owner relaying tasks over Discord daily. Delegation stops being a chat thread.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> ops.php + cc.php ownerType/assignee layer, Magnamus login pattern</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="approval inbox — approvals.php on the bridge.php protocol new studio page where every ai-produced deliverable (translated scripts, faf scripts, drafted patreon replies, social captions, redactor re-releases) lands as a pending card with approve / edit / reject buttons; approving marks a bridge.php job &#x27;done&#x27; and routes the artifact to the executor&#x27;s queue (usually alternate for posting). rejections capture a one-line reason that gets appended to the relevant pipeline-skill lesson file. this is the cheap-supervision layer the whole transition hinges on: owner spends ~10 min/day approving instead of producing, ai output never publishes unsupervised (matches the never-post-without-permission rule), and rejection reasons compound into better prompts."><summary><span class="t">Approval Inbox — approvals.php on the bridge.php protocol</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>New studio page where every AI-produced deliverable (translated scripts, FAF scripts, drafted Patreon replies, social captions, Redactor re-releases) lands as a pending card with Approve / Edit / Reject buttons; approving marks a bridge.php job &#x27;done&#x27; and routes the artifact to the executor&#x27;s queue (usually Alternate for posting). Rejections capture a one-line reason that gets appended to the relevant pipeline-skill lesson file.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> This is the cheap-supervision layer the whole transition hinges on: owner spends ~10 min/day approving instead of producing, AI output never publishes unsupervised (matches the never-post-without-permission rule), and rejection reasons compound into better prompts.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php claim/done verbs + cc.php + studio login</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="gwhar story-scout intake feeding the missing ideator stage build studio/scout.php: a dead-simple form where gwhar submits story finds (link or premise, why it works, growth-potential 1-5, which property it fits: growgetter/maxx/bloom). each submission triggers a bridge.php job that runs the script-breakdown skill to expand it into a one-page premise + beat sheet, which lands in the approval inbox for the owner to greenlight into production. fills the ideator gap in the 7-stage vision with a $100-200/mo human whose hobby literally is finding stories, and gives the proven autonomous production line (44-panel overnight run) a queue of vetted premises to eat."><summary><span class="t">GWHAR story-scout intake feeding the missing ideator stage</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Build studio/scout.php: a dead-simple form where GWHAR submits story finds (link or premise, why it works, growth-potential 1-5, which property it fits: GrowGetter/Maxx/Bloom). Each submission triggers a bridge.php job that runs the script-breakdown skill to expand it into a one-page premise + beat sheet, which lands in the Approval Inbox for the owner to greenlight into production.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Fills the ideator gap in the 7-stage vision with a $100-200/mo human whose hobby literally is finding stories, and gives the proven autonomous production line (44-panel overnight run) a queue of vetted premises to eat.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php + script-breakdown skill + Approval Inbox; fills &#x27;ideator&#x27; gap</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="patreon message/comment triage with ai-drafted replies extend the creator pulse daily sync on the mac mini to also pull messages and comments from the 4 patreon accounts, classify each (spam / commission inquiry / fan mail / support issue), and draft a reply in the house voice. drafts land in the approval inbox; spam gets a one-click &#x27;confirm delete&#x27; list; commission inquiries get flagged straight to the owner with the thread context attached. sending stays human (alternate pastes approved replies). replaces three magna duties at once (answer messages, answer comments, clear spam across maxx/bloom/growgetter) — the single biggest daily-touch chunk of his $1,500 — while keeping every outbound message human-approved."><summary><span class="t">Patreon message/comment triage with AI-drafted replies</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Extend the Creator Pulse daily sync on the Mac mini to also pull messages and comments from the 4 Patreon accounts, classify each (spam / commission inquiry / fan mail / support issue), and draft a reply in the house voice. Drafts land in the Approval Inbox; spam gets a one-click &#x27;confirm delete&#x27; list; commission inquiries get flagged straight to the owner with the thread context attached. Sending stays human (Alternate pastes approved replies).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Replaces three Magna duties at once (answer messages, answer comments, clear spam across Maxx/Bloom/GrowGetter) — the single biggest daily-touch chunk of his $1,500 — while keeping every outbound message human-approved.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse Mac mini sync + Approval Inbox</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="translation assembly line as a bridge.php job kind codify the existing sop (strip script to dialogue-only → ai translate es/de/zh → upwork proofread) as a new bridge.php job kind &#x27;translate&#x27;: worker strips dialogue from the script, ai translates all three languages, outputs a proofreader-ready doc plus a pre-drafted upwork message; the send-to-proofreader step surfaces as a gwhar queue task, and returned proofs flow to page-composer for re-lettering. the same job kind powers comic redactor re-releases of &gt;6-month-old comics. turns two recurring magna duties (growgetter translation, sending to proofreaders) into a fire-and-forget job the owner never touches except at approval, and unblocks the seo-driven redactor back-catalog at scale."><summary><span class="t">Translation assembly line as a bridge.php job kind</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">AI</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Codify the existing SOP (strip script to dialogue-only → AI translate ES/DE/ZH → Upwork proofread) as a new bridge.php job kind &#x27;translate&#x27;: worker strips dialogue from the script, AI translates all three languages, outputs a proofreader-ready doc plus a pre-drafted Upwork message; the send-to-proofreader step surfaces as a GWHAR queue task, and returned proofs flow to page-composer for re-lettering. The same job kind powers Comic Redactor re-releases of &gt;6-month-old comics.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns two recurring Magna duties (GrowGetter translation, sending to proofreaders) into a fire-and-forget job the owner never touches except at approval, and unblocks the SEO-driven Redactor back-catalog at scale.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php job kinds (adjust/transform) + page-composer skill + Comic Redactor duty SOP</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="recurring-duty respawner cron on the mac mini the &#x27;runner on bridge.php&#x27; is still concept-only — ship its simplest useful slice: a cron on the mac mini (which already runs the creator pulse daily sync) that reads a recurrence field on cc.php duties (weekly publish, weekly faf, monthly sketches, monthly bloom/maxx scripts) and respawns each as a fresh dated task in the right person&#x27;s queue, pinging a discord webhook to the assignee. overdue respawns escalate to the owner after 48h. nothing recurring silently drops during the transition — the #1 way delegation handoffs fail. the owner stops being the human cron job that remembers what&#x27;s due."><summary><span class="t">Recurring-duty respawner cron on the Mac mini</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The &#x27;runner on bridge.php&#x27; is still concept-only — ship its simplest useful slice: a cron on the Mac mini (which already runs the Creator Pulse daily sync) that reads a recurrence field on cc.php duties (weekly publish, weekly FAF, monthly sketches, monthly Bloom/Maxx scripts) and respawns each as a fresh dated task in the right person&#x27;s queue, pinging a Discord webhook to the assignee. Overdue respawns escalate to the owner after 48h.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Nothing recurring silently drops during the transition — the #1 way delegation handoffs fail. The owner stops being the human cron job that remembers what&#x27;s due.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Mac mini cron (Creator Pulse pattern) + cc.php + ownership layer</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="alternate&#x27;s post-packet generator for every publish/share task (weekly comic, monthly sketches across all patreons, da/discord shares), a bridge.php job assembles a self-contained packet page in the studio: final images in upload order, per-platform caption text (da vs twitter vs discord character limits and tag conventions), title, tags, and a tick-box checklist. alternate opens the packet from their queue view and just uploads — zero judgment calls required. makes low-cost posting labor reliable (fewer wrong-caption/wrong-account errors across 4 patreon accounts + da + discord) and produces exactly the paste-ready payloads the deferred syndicator stage will automate later — a stepping stone, not throwaway work."><summary><span class="t">Alternate&#x27;s post-packet generator</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>For every publish/share task (weekly comic, monthly sketches across all Patreons, DA/Discord shares), a bridge.php job assembles a self-contained packet page in the studio: final images in upload order, per-platform caption text (DA vs Twitter vs Discord character limits and tag conventions), title, tags, and a tick-box checklist. Alternate opens the packet from their queue view and just uploads — zero judgment calls required.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Makes low-cost posting labor reliable (fewer wrong-caption/wrong-account errors across 4 Patreon accounts + DA + Discord) and produces exactly the paste-ready payloads the deferred syndicator stage will automate later — a stepping stone, not throwaway work.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php + per-person queue views; stepping stone to the deferred syndicator stage</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="transition budget tracker vs the $1,500 baseline add a small ledger section to cc.php (or a creator pulse tab): a json file of monthly spend per replacement channel — gwhar, alternate, upwork proofreaders, higgsfield credits, misc ai costs — charted against the $1,500 magna baseline, with a duties-covered checklist beside it (12/15 rerouted, 3 pending). updated by a 2-minute monthly entry or receipts dropped in a folder the mac mini sync ingests. makes the transition&#x27;s core bet visible weekly: are we actually under $1,500 with all 15 duties covered, and which channel is creeping. catches &#x27;cheap labor + credits quietly cost more than magna&#x27; before it compounds."><summary><span class="t">Transition budget tracker vs the $1,500 baseline</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:owner</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a small ledger section to cc.php (or a Creator Pulse tab): a JSON file of monthly spend per replacement channel — GWHAR, Alternate, Upwork proofreaders, Higgsfield credits, misc AI costs — charted against the $1,500 Magna baseline, with a duties-covered checklist beside it (12/15 rerouted, 3 pending). Updated by a 2-minute monthly entry or receipts dropped in a folder the Mac mini sync ingests.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Makes the transition&#x27;s core bet visible weekly: are we actually under $1,500 with all 15 duties covered, and which channel is creeping. Catches &#x27;cheap labor + credits quietly cost more than Magna&#x27; before it compounds.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> cc.php + Creator Pulse dashboard</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="delegation" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="weekly piracy sweep as a scheduled task a weekly scheduled job (mac mini cron or a scheduled claude task) that searches google and the known-active allporncomix forum for growgetter/maxx/bloom titles and recent release names, diffs against last week&#x27;s hits, and files any new hit as a cc.php task with the infringing url, screenshot, and a pre-filled dmca template attached — assigned to the owner for the actual send. converts the &#x27;monitor piracy&#x27; magna duty into a 5-minute-a-week owner review instead of an ongoing vigilance job, and creates a timestamped evidence log for repeat infringers."><summary><span class="t">Weekly piracy sweep as a scheduled task</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Delegation</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A weekly scheduled job (Mac mini cron or a scheduled Claude task) that searches Google and the known-active Allporncomix forum for GrowGetter/Maxx/Bloom titles and recent release names, diffs against last week&#x27;s hits, and files any new hit as a cc.php task with the infringing URL, screenshot, and a pre-filled DMCA template attached — assigned to the owner for the actual send.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Converts the &#x27;monitor piracy&#x27; Magna duty into a 5-minute-a-week owner review instead of an ongoing vigilance job, and creates a timestamped evidence log for repeat infringers.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Mac mini cron + cc.php task creation; covers duty #15 of the Magna list</p></div></details></section><section class="grp" data-grp="tooling"><h3>Studio UX <span class="n">9</span></h3><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="morning brief card at the top of command center (cc.php) add a digest panel that renders first when cc.php loads: overnight bridge.php job outcomes (claimed/done/failed counts per batch), flow-studio-autosync ingest count, ck_ai_qa defects flagged, creator pulse deltas from the mac mini&#x27;s daily sync (new/lost patrons per account), and today&#x27;s due tasks by ownertype. a small cron on the mac mini assembles a brief.json each morning; cc.php just renders it with deep links into creator.php batches and ops.php tasks. since the autonomous 44-panel overnight run proved unattended production works, this is the missing &#x27;what happened while i slept&#x27; surface. turns the first 30-45 minutes of manual checking (flow tab, studio batches, pulse, task board) into one 60-second read with links straight to anything needing a decision."><summary><span class="t">Morning Brief card at the top of Command Center (cc.php)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a digest panel that renders first when cc.php loads: overnight bridge.php job outcomes (claimed/done/failed counts per batch), flow-studio-autosync ingest count, ck_ai_qa defects flagged, Creator Pulse deltas from the Mac mini&#x27;s daily sync (new/lost patrons per account), and today&#x27;s due tasks by ownerType. A small cron on the Mac mini assembles a brief.json each morning; cc.php just renders it with deep links into creator.php batches and ops.php tasks. Since the autonomous 44-panel overnight run proved unattended production works, this is the missing &#x27;what happened while I slept&#x27; surface.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Turns the first 30-45 minutes of manual checking (Flow tab, Studio batches, Pulse, task board) into one 60-second read with links straight to anything needing a decision.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> cc.php, bridge.php, Creator Pulse daily sync, flow-studio-autosync, ck_ai_qa</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="unified discord webhook notifier (studio/inc/notify.php) one tiny helper function every studio system calls to post to a private discord server with per-severity channels: #done (bridge.php job completed, autosync ingested n panels, deploy finished), #needs-you (qa defect flagged, worker heartbeat lost &gt;10min, pulse sync failed), #alerts (deploy hash mismatch, login anomalies). wire it into bridge.php&#x27;s done/heartbeat verbs, creator.php&#x27;s qa scan, and deploy_3dmc.sh in one pass. discord is already in the distribution stack, so the owner gets pings on his phone with zero new apps. kills polling entirely — overnight runs and worker stalls surface as push notifications instead of being discovered hours later, and failed runs stop wasting a night."><summary><span class="t">Unified Discord webhook notifier (studio/inc/notify.php)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>One tiny helper function every Studio system calls to post to a private Discord server with per-severity channels: #done (bridge.php job completed, autosync ingested N panels, deploy finished), #needs-you (QA defect flagged, worker heartbeat lost &gt;10min, Pulse sync failed), #alerts (deploy hash mismatch, login anomalies). Wire it into bridge.php&#x27;s done/heartbeat verbs, creator.php&#x27;s QA scan, and deploy_3dmc.sh in one pass. Discord is already in the distribution stack, so the owner gets pings on his phone with zero new apps.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Kills polling entirely — overnight runs and worker stalls surface as push notifications instead of being discovered hours later, and failed runs stop wasting a night.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> bridge.php, creator.php QA scan, deploy_3dmc.sh, Creator Pulse</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="mobile one-thumb rate mode for review.php add a phone-optimized mode to the existing review.php: full-screen panel image, big tap zones (keep / trash-to-subfolder / retry-as-adjust-job), swipe to advance, pinch-zoom for defect checking. reuses the exact rating semantics of the keyboard-rate loop and the trash-subfolder convention, and &#x27;retry&#x27; composes a bridge.php kind=adjust job inline. progress bar shows batch position so a 44-panel overnight batch is clearable in one sitting. the single biggest human bottleneck — rating overnight batches — moves off the desk to couch/commute time; a 40-panel batch triages in ~5 minutes from a phone."><summary><span class="t">Mobile one-thumb rate mode for review.php</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:Owner</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Add a phone-optimized mode to the existing review.php: full-screen panel image, big tap zones (keep / trash-to-subfolder / retry-as-adjust-job), swipe to advance, pinch-zoom for defect checking. Reuses the exact rating semantics of the keyboard-rate loop and the trash-subfolder convention, and &#x27;retry&#x27; composes a bridge.php kind=adjust job inline. Progress bar shows batch position so a 44-panel overnight batch is clearable in one sitting.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The single biggest human bottleneck — rating overnight batches — moves off the desk to couch/commute time; a 40-panel batch triages in ~5 minutes from a phone.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> review.php, keyboard-rate loop, bridge.php adjust jobs, trash-subfolder convention</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="shared studio nav + cmd-k command palette (studio/inc/nav.php) a single header include adopted by all ~15 studio pages (creator, import, ops, cc, attribution, pulse, review, growgetter...) plus links out to /admin/ cms and the live site. cmd-k opens a palette that fuzzy-searches pages, cc tasks by number/title, and comic projects, plus quick actions: &#x27;new adjust job&#x27;, &#x27;run qa scan on latest batch&#x27;, &#x27;open latest autosync ingest&#x27;. pure php+js, no framework. every session currently starts with url-typing and tab archaeology across a sprawling studio; the palette makes any section or task 2 keystrokes away and makes cc.php the genuine home page."><summary><span class="t">Shared Studio nav + Cmd-K command palette (studio/inc/nav.php)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Human:Owner</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>A single header include adopted by all ~15 studio pages (creator, import, ops, cc, attribution, pulse, review, growgetter...) plus links out to /admin/ CMS and the live site. Cmd-K opens a palette that fuzzy-searches pages, CC tasks by number/title, and comic projects, plus quick actions: &#x27;new adjust job&#x27;, &#x27;run QA scan on latest batch&#x27;, &#x27;open latest autosync ingest&#x27;. Pure PHP+JS, no framework.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Every session currently starts with URL-typing and tab archaeology across a sprawling studio; the palette makes any section or task 2 keystrokes away and makes cc.php the genuine home page.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> studio/inc shared includes, cc.php/ops.php task data, all existing studio pages</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="L" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="cockpit v1: brief-to-worker-to-winner loop in creator.php ship the minimal version of the already-envisioned comic-creator cockpit: a brief form on creator.php (premise, cast refs to attach, panel count, stage/tier notes) that writes a genspec through bridge.php&#x27;s existing verbs; worker.py picks it up; results stream back into a winner-picker grid where one click promotes a variant as the ref-chain parent for the next beat. no new protocol needed — bridge.php&#x27;s claim/genspec/heartbeat/done already covers it; this is ui plus a genspec composer that bakes in the pipeline&#x27;s codified lessons (ref attachment, wardrobe lock, lettering). generation stops requiring a local claude session driving flow by hand — the owner (or later gwhar) can launch and steer a comic run from any browser, which is the core unlock for scaling past one operator."><summary><span class="t">Cockpit v1: brief-to-worker-to-winner loop in creator.php</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort L</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Ship the minimal version of the already-envisioned comic-creator cockpit: a brief form on creator.php (premise, cast refs to attach, panel count, stage/tier notes) that writes a genspec through bridge.php&#x27;s existing verbs; worker.py picks it up; results stream back into a winner-picker grid where one click promotes a variant as the ref-chain parent for the next beat. No new protocol needed — bridge.php&#x27;s claim/genspec/heartbeat/done already covers it; this is UI plus a genspec composer that bakes in the pipeline&#x27;s codified lessons (ref attachment, wardrobe lock, lettering).</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Generation stops requiring a local Claude session driving Flow by hand — the owner (or later GWHAR) can launch and steer a comic run from any browser, which is the core unlock for scaling past one operator.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> creator.php, bridge.php worker protocol, worker.py, comic-production skill lessons</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="one-click &#x27;fix it&#x27; on every qa defect flag the ck_ai_qa scan in creator.php already flags defects (duplicate characters/extras as priority). add a button per flag that auto-composes a bridge.php kind=adjust job: correction prompt templated from the defect type (e.g. &#x27;remove background extras, cast count must be n&#x27;), parent panel attached as ref, stage-aware character refs included. result lands back next to the original with a compare view. closes the loop from detection to repair — defects currently found by ai still cost a manual prompt-writing round-trip; this makes each fix one click and reuses the exact failure-mode prompts already codified in the pipeline&#x27;s 35 lessons."><summary><span class="t">One-click &#x27;Fix it&#x27; on every QA defect flag</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>The ck_ai_qa scan in creator.php already flags defects (duplicate characters/extras as priority). Add a button per flag that auto-composes a bridge.php kind=adjust job: correction prompt templated from the defect type (e.g. &#x27;remove background extras, cast count must be N&#x27;), parent panel attached as ref, stage-aware character refs included. Result lands back next to the original with a compare view.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Closes the loop from detection to repair — defects currently found by AI still cost a manual prompt-writing round-trip; this makes each fix one click and reuses the exact failure-mode prompts already codified in the pipeline&#x27;s 35 lessons.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> creator.php ck_ai_qa, bridge.php adjust jobs, comic-production failure-mode lessons</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="&#x27;run with ai&#x27; button on command center tasks tasks in cc.php/ops.php already carry aitag/aiplan (&#x27;how ai would do this&#x27;) and the new ownertype field. add a button on ai-owned tasks that executes the aiplan: v1 copies a fully-formed self-contained prompt (aiplan + task context + relevant file paths) to clipboard for pasting into a claude session; v2 posts it as a bridge.php job for the always-on runner already planned on bridge.php. completion writes a timestamped board note back to the task, matching the batch-1 posted-as-board-notes pattern. the 388-task backlog with magna leaving becomes executable, not just triaged — each ai-owned task goes from &#x27;someday&#x27; to a one-click dispatch, directly absorbing part of the $1,500/mo of duties."><summary><span class="t">&#x27;Run with AI&#x27; button on Command Center tasks</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Tasks in cc.php/ops.php already carry aiTag/aiPlan (&#x27;how AI would do this&#x27;) and the new ownerType field. Add a button on AI-owned tasks that executes the aiPlan: v1 copies a fully-formed self-contained prompt (aiPlan + task context + relevant file paths) to clipboard for pasting into a Claude session; v2 posts it as a bridge.php job for the always-on runner already planned on bridge.php. Completion writes a timestamped board note back to the task, matching the Batch-1 posted-as-board-notes pattern.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> The 388-task backlog with Magna leaving becomes executable, not just triaged — each AI-owned task goes from &#x27;someday&#x27; to a one-click dispatch, directly absorbing part of the $1,500/mo of duties.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> cc.php/ops.php aiPlan fields, ownerType layer, bridge.php runner concept</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="S" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="deploy guard in deploy_3dmc.sh against concurrent-session clobber extend tools/deploy_3dmc.sh with a pre-upload check: fetch the live file, compare its hash against the hash recorded at the session&#x27;s fetch-live step (stored in a .deploy-state file), and hard-stop with a diff summary if the live copy changed since — exactly the creator.php clobber that already bit parallel sessions. also stamp a version+timestamp comment into each deployed php header so &#x27;which version is live&#x27; is answerable at a glance. eliminates a documented recurring hazard where one session silently destroys another&#x27;s live feature; recovery from a clobber costs hours, prevention costs one hash comparison."><summary><span class="t">Deploy guard in deploy_3dmc.sh against concurrent-session clobber</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort S</span><span class="chip c-own">System</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Extend tools/deploy_3dmc.sh with a pre-upload check: fetch the live file, compare its hash against the hash recorded at the session&#x27;s fetch-live step (stored in a .deploy-state file), and hard-stop with a diff summary if the live copy changed since — exactly the creator.php clobber that already bit parallel sessions. Also stamp a version+timestamp comment into each deployed PHP header so &#x27;which version is live&#x27; is answerable at a glance.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Eliminates a documented recurring hazard where one session silently destroys another&#x27;s live feature; recovery from a clobber costs hours, prevention costs one hash comparison.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> tools/deploy_3dmc.sh, the fetch-live-before-editing rule, CHANGELOG.md convention</p></div></details><details class="idea" data-lens="tooling" data-eff="M" data-hor="" data-wave="1" data-rev="0" data-hay="unified patreon inbox with ai-drafted replies (studio/inbox.php) extend the creator pulse mac-mini sync (it already authenticates to all 4 patreon accounts daily) to also pull unread messages and post comments into one queue page in studio. each item shows an ai-drafted reply the owner can edit and copy — drafting only, sending stays manual per the never-post-without-permission rule. include a spam bucket with one-tap dismiss for the maxx/bloom/growgetter spam-clearing duty. two of magna&#x27;s recurring duties (answer messages/comments, clear spam) collapse from logging into 4 accounts daily to one 10-minute studio pass with pre-written drafts."><summary><span class="t">Unified Patreon inbox with AI-drafted replies (studio/inbox.php)</span><span class="chips"><span class="chip c-lens">Studio UX</span><span class="chip c-eff">effort M</span><span class="chip c-own">Hybrid</span></span></summary><div class="b"><p>Extend the Creator Pulse Mac-mini sync (it already authenticates to all 4 Patreon accounts daily) to also pull unread messages and post comments into one queue page in Studio. Each item shows an AI-drafted reply the owner can edit and copy — drafting only, sending stays manual per the never-post-without-permission rule. Include a spam bucket with one-tap dismiss for the Maxx/Bloom/GrowGetter spam-clearing duty.</p><p class="impact"><strong>Impact:</strong> Two of Magna&#x27;s recurring duties (answer messages/comments, clear spam) collapse from logging into 4 accounts daily to one 10-minute studio pass with pre-written drafts.</p><p class="builds"><strong>Builds on:</strong> Creator Pulse 4-account sync, studio login gate, ownership-layer duty list</p></div></details></section>
</div>
<script>
const F={};const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('.idea')];const grps=[...document.querySelectorAll('.grp')];
const q=document.getElementById('q');const cnt=document.getElementById('count');
function apply(){const s=q.value.toLowerCase().trim();let n=0;
cards.forEach(c=>{let ok=true;
for(const[k,v]of Object.entries(F)){if(v&&c.dataset[k]!==v)ok=false}
if(s&&!c.dataset.hay.includes(s))ok=false;
c.classList.toggle('hide',!ok);if(ok)n++});
grps.forEach(g=>g.classList.toggle('hide',!g.querySelector('.idea:not(.hide)')));
cnt.textContent=n+' / '+cards.length}
document.getElementById('filters').addEventListener('click',ev=>{const f=ev.target.closest('.f');if(!f)return;
const k=f.dataset.k,v=f.dataset.v;
if(F[k]===v){F[k]='';f.classList.remove('on')}else{F[k]=v;document.querySelectorAll(`.f[data-k="${k}"]`).forEach(x=>x.classList.remove('on'));f.classList.add('on')}
apply()});
q.addEventListener('input',apply);apply();
</script>
</body>
